nkedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T12:54:10-07:00","id":882122,"title":"","content":"Hi guys, found my first doubts in the first 5 minutes <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> -Does <b>Matter Mage Armor</b> stacks with <b>Aegis </b>(Matter 3, p.156) spell?<br /> <br /> - <b>Death Mage Armor</b> (p.193), when it speaks about wounds, do you mean Health Levels or individual sources of damage?. In other words, If I have Death 3 Mage Armor and some one shoots me dealing 5 Lethal Health Levels, Do I have 5 bashing wounds or 2 Lethal and 3 bashing?<br /> <br /> - <b>Fate Mage Armor</b> (p.194), The bonus damage is applied to mundane attacks? spells? aimed spells?.<br /> <br /> - Also, can you dispell (not counter a spell being cast, but dispelling a working spell) a Mind spell using Mind arcanum? or you need the <b>Dispel Magic</b> spell (p.165)?<br /> EDIT: yes, you need Dispel Magic.<br /> <br /> More soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3008-masa","user":"Masa","date":". 05-05-2016, 03:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3008-masa","name":"Masa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3008_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T12:58:22-07:00","id":882131,"title":"","content":"I remember seeing it during development but is the old 'create familiar' spell from 1e an attainment or is it just gained by purchasing the merit?<br /> <br /> I ask because I can't seem to find anything on how to a familiar is gained though I admit I've only had time to scim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T13:05:21-07:00","id":882144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/880060-awakening-second-edition-faq-thread?p=882131#post882131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember seeing it during development but is the old 'create familiar' spell from 1e an attainment or is it just gained by purchasing the merit?<br /> <br /> I ask because I can't seem to find anything on how to a familiar is gained though I admit I've only had time to scim.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's both a Merit and a Spirit 4 spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T13:11:46-07:00","id":882151,"title":"","content":"The Merit represents having had the spell cast on you, made indefinite, and relinquished, presumably by a mentor as its a patterning spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T13:25:53-07:00","id":882167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/880060-awakening-second-edition-faq-thread?p=882144#post882144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's both a Merit and a Spirit 4 spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Had not thought to look under spirit since I was thinking of binding a ghost. Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T13:33:59-07:00","id":882178,"title":"","content":"How does a mage set spell factors and reach when imbuing a spell into an item? Thanks! (This book is so cool.)<br /> Page 196","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T13:56:06-07:00","id":882199,"title":"","content":"So. Zombies. Yes, I' m pretty much only devouring Death things right now.<br /> Potency makes Zombies act like Retainers. Retainers have a natural ceiling of 5. Creative Thaumaturgy mentions that you need to pay Mana in order to breakthrough natural Trait limitations (and Merits are Traits). So, if I want to create that GigaMega ZombieBro with Potency 1000000, do I have to pay Mana for going past 5? <br /> <br /> Is it safe to assume that products of Death Spells that create things out of ephemera or Shadows, and have static value of 2 where game traits are concerned, can have these traits modified by Improvised Death Spells following Creative Thaumaturgy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T14:07:14-07:00","id":882211,"title":"","content":"How does one use Mind to give Goetia the ability to possess people? It says it's possible in the book, but unless I missed something big on my readthrough of Mind, it doesn't actually give you a writeup for how it should work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T14:10:29-07:00","id":882217,"title":"","content":"I Turn Him Into A Frog sidebar at page 127 very explicitly states that Unmaking Spells ALWAYS are subject to being Withstood. I understand that this means that you cannot bypass Witshanding with Exceptional Success on these spells, nor the target can willingly let the spell in?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 05-04-2016, 06:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T14:17:58-07:00","id":882223,"title":"","content":"When using Hung Spell (p.187-188) by cancelling the spell, is it all or nothing, or can you selectively decide to fire off specific spells? What if you downgrade the Potency, mentioned in p.118? If you use the Conditional Duration attainment with Hung Spell, can you select different triggers for different spells, or is it also all or nothing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T14:49:27-07:00","id":882255,"title":"","content":"More questions!<br /> <br /> <br /> The Spells Shifting the Odds and Strings of Fate mention a time frame between hours and days for the effects of the spell to ocurr, however it doesn't say if you need to keep the duraction active for that whole time frame or if the spell makes some &quot;lasting&quot; changes that enable the circumstances to pass after the spell ends. If not, the only way for the spell to work is to Reach. How do these spells work?<br /> <br /> <br /> In Psychic Domination (p. 161), why is Reach used to give the target extra actions or tasks to complete? Shouldn't it be one action / task per Potency instead? Will the subject stop performing a Task when the Duration of the spell expires? Other spells that give subjects commands specify it but this one doesn't.<br /> <br /> <br /> If I where to create a Mind Knowing spell that alerts me to the presence of minds in the area of the spell, similar to Web of Life (p. 148) how would it interact with ghosts, spirits, Goetia, Supernal Beings, etc? <br /> <br /> <br /> Can I touch an animal and use Speak with Beasts on it to make it speak another animal's language? Could I make that animal speak a Human language? If not, could I do it in combination with Mind 3?<br /> <br /> <br /> Have you noticed that it is easier to Summon a Rank 5 Spirit across the Gauntlet (requires Potency 6) than cure a drug overdose (requires Potency 8)? <br /> <br /> <br /> During Duel Arcane, do I need to spend the 1 Reach for instant casting every single attack to make it instant cast?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T16:50:00-07:00","id":882345,"title":"","content":"Okay, so this one had been bugging me. If you have a rote and praxis of the same spell, do you have to choose between casting it as a rote or praxis, or do you do both?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8509-ketharuil","name":"Ketharuil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T16:57:20-07:00","id":882350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ketharuil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/880060-awakening-second-edition-faq-thread?p=882345#post882345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so this one had been bugging me. If you have a rote and praxis of the same spell, do you have to choose between casting it as a rote or praxis, or do you do both?</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 112: The benefits of Rotes do not stack with the benefits of Praxes. If a mage has the same spell as both a Rote and a Praxis, she must decide at casting which she uses. Rotes may be purchased for one Experience each, and the character must be capable of casting the spell as an improvised spell before purchasing the Rote.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T17:04:43-07:00","id":882356,"title":"","content":"P. 143: &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">This spell can also be used to alter the tone of a given sound,<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"> including modifying a target\u2019s voice to sound like another. Emulating a specific voice might require an Expression + Subterfuge<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"> roll to get it right.&quot;</span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> Is that supposed to be an Attribute and one of those two skills?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently playing at Fabula Rasa in the Cold Equations venue; planning an Obrimos for Fallen London.<br /> I can also be found at <a href=\"http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com\" target=\"_blank\">http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2192-heu","name":"Heu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T17:17:43-07:00","id":882364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/880060-awakening-second-edition-faq-thread?p=882350#post882350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Page 112: The benefits of Rotes do not stack with the benefits of Praxes. If a mage has the same spell as both a Rote and a Praxis, she must decide at casting which she uses. Rotes may be purchased for one Experience each, and the character must be capable of casting the spell as an improvised spell before purchasing the Rote.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, Jakki. Missed that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8509-ketharuil","name":"Ketharuil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T17:24:07-07:00","id":882367,"title":"","content":"So, although not all Arcanum gave instant kill spells, they all have that as a possibility, right? Miracle for fate gives struck by lightning as an example, since it's mentioned to be an instant kill in another part of the book. Time could, say, with temporal Sympathy, unmake someone's birth? Mind unmake their mind itself?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8509-ketharuil","name":"Ketharuil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T17:29:51-07:00","id":882371,"title":"","content":"Can a mage visit the Temenos with the correct level of Mind and Spirit, and ask Perry the Platypus to become his familiar? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T17:51:25-07:00","id":882388,"title":"","content":"Most of the spells so far (I'm up to Matter) look pretty solid, but then we have Matter and I'm left wondering what the hell happened. There's a spell to determine where hidden things are and if you add Forces it involves also finding electronic data on a device. Couldn't just straight Forces accomplish the same effect?<br /> <br /> Also, Shrink Object mentions that if you add Life 3 you can use this spell to effect living things, but shouldn't that be a straight function of Life? Why is Matter needed to shrink living beings?<br /> <br /> Death 4 allows you to change into living shadows without Life conjunction, Matter 4 does not grant the same. Isn't this inconsistent?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 05-04-2016, 09:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T18:55:37-07:00","id":882422,"title":"","content":"How does a mage cross into the shadow? I've seen spells to raise or lower the gauntlet or some that reference a mage interacting from either side. I guess it may be more accurate to asl what spirit arcana rating would a mage require to enter the shadow?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T19:50:06-07:00","id":882463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/880060-awakening-second-edition-faq-thread?p=882422#post882422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does a mage cross into the shadow? I've seen spells to raise or lower the gauntlet or some that reference a mage interacting from either side. I guess it may be more accurate to asl what spirit arcana rating would a mage require to enter the shadow?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't want to step on Dave's toes, but take a look at World Walker (Spirit 4, p. 184) and the Reach effect for Reaching (Spirit 3, p. 182). Both spells explicitly provide direct access to the Shadow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T21:15:50-07:00","id":882518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/880060-awakening-second-edition-faq-thread?p=882463#post882463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I don't want to step on Dave's toes, but take a look at World Walker (Spirit 4, p. 184) and the Reach effect for Reaching (Spirit 3, p. 182). Both spells explicitly provide direct access to the Shadow.</div> </div> </div> </div>D'oh thank you","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T22:14:20-07:00","id":882560,"title":"","content":"Some confusion on Active Mage Sight - On general rules states that character's &quot;Sight won\u2019t let her see through walls or perceive entities and objects in a state of Twilight. &quot; But when we look in to Death and Spirit they can see Manifested ones - and one of Manifestation is Twilight Form, most basic one. So Active Mage Sight can or cannot see beings in Twilight?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-05-2016, 01:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T00:22:21-07:00","id":882634,"title":"","content":"Does Paths of Soul Stones use in creation of Demesnes is important? Or any combination is permitted? Creating Demesnes from Soul Stones of the same Path is easier?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T00:39:33-07:00","id":882641,"title":"","content":"I'm still digging-down on many parts of this magical tome, but my list of questions, concerns and pleas for advice has become quite substantial. I thought I might as well post what I have thus far.<br /> <br /> <u>Forces Questions</u>:<br /> <br /> Can Forces be used to control mechanical items like Matter?<br /> <br /> Can a Life 4 / Forces 4 spell transmute a target into a living force?<br /> <br /> Why is Potency the Primary Factor for Forces 2 Control Gravity when the level Potency does not affect the spell. Shouldn't it be Duration (or Scale-Area of Effect)?<br /> <br /> If telekinesis and gravity control only require 3 dots of Forces, why does levitation require 4?<br /> <br /> Can Forces 2 Control Gravity (or Forces Ruling) negate Falling damage? If not, what Practice is required?<br /> <br /> Can Forces 3 Turn Momentum (or Forces Weaving) also be used against physical Weaponry and Brawl attacks?<br /> <br /> Was the omission of kinetic energy, gravity and radiation on the Transform Energy chart (p.146) intentional or an oversight? Can kinetic energy, gravity and radiation (and other forces) also be transformed with the spell?<br /> <br /> Can Transform Energy (or Forces Patterning or Weaving) transform any one force into actual sunlight, such as would harm vampires?<br /> <br /> Why does Forces 5 Adverse Weather require a Reach to drastically change weather different from local conditions when the spell explicitly is not supposed to be limited by the constraints of Forces 2 Control Weather?<br /> <br /> Forces 5 Adverse Weather claims to create Extreme Environments up to Level 5. However, according to p. 224, EE only goes up to 4. Is this correct? If so, is this the Forces equivalent of turning an amp &quot;up to eleven&quot; and creating Hiroshima-levels of destruction? (Would a hypothetical Forces 6 Dynamics spell go all the way to EE 6 and with a larger area of effect?)<br /> <br /> Forces 5 - Earthquake: Does a mage need spend Reach and dice penalties to increase Scale (size or area of affect) in order to damage buildings and other structures or is that already inherent to the spell?<br /> <br /> If additional Duration is added to Earthquake, will damage to buildings\u2019 Structure accrue each turn (or other time interval)?<br /> <br /> Why doesn't Earthquake also inflict the Earthquake Tilt along with the property damage?<br /> <br /> Can a Forces mage inflict the Earthquake or most other Environmental Tilts as spells similar to Matter 2 Shaping (but possibly without Matter\u2019s need for extra Reach?<br /> <br /> Does Forces use Extreme Environment (p. 224) as its default levels to affect the environment or the various Environmental Tilts (p. 319-324)? A review of the Forces spells appear to indicate a consistent use of EE, while other Arcana such as Matter consistently only use the provided Tilts. Is there some guideline to know when a spell should use EE vs. a indicated Environmental Tilt?<br /> <br /> What Practices of Forces are necessary to create realistic audio and visual (and tactile) illusions? Would such spells need to be cast as combined spells to achieve all the sensory effects, or a single spell, possibly with some added Reach?<br /> <br /> Can Forces 2 Shielding provide an absolute defense to energy attacks, including kinetic energy (e.g., bullets and melee weaponry), or would such effects be limited to an armor rating similar to the Forces Attainment Armor, requires some form of Clash of Wills, etc.?<br /> <br /> Unlike Turn Momentum, can a Forces Practice be used provide an absolute defense similar to Turn Momentum while still allowing the mage actions other than Dodging during a turn?<br /> <br /> What Practice of Forces, if any, can be used to create ballistic armor? Would it just be Reach effect for a Shielding spell?<br /> <br /> What Arcana and Practices do you need to hack into and read, alter and control computers, cell phones and other electronics items? If a mage wants hack wirelessly/remotely, can he just use Forces (e.g., wireless transmission) or must it be done via sympathetic casting?<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> What Practice of Forces is used to choke or grapple a target (i.e., the Darth Vader move)?<br /> [It's the perfect Rote for an Obrimos - &quot;Your Lack of Faith Is Disturbing&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ]<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 05-05-2016, 04:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T00:50:20-07:00","id":882647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/880060-awakening-second-edition-faq-thread?p=882641#post882641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still digging-down on many parts of this magical tome, but my list of questions, concerns and pleas for advice has become quite substantial. I thought I might as well post what I have thus far.<br /> <br /> <u>Forces Questions</u>:<br /> <br /> What Arcana and Practices do you need to hack into and read, alter and control computers, cell phones and other electronics items? If a mage wants hack wirelessly/remotely, can he just use Forces (e.g., wireless transmission) or must it be done via sympathetic casting?<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is the only one of your questions I know the answer to, yes hacking into, reading, altering and controlling electronics and computers in their typical functionality is mostly forces (some stuff can also easily be time or matter). To hack wirelessly (so in the same area) it's just done by spending a reach to cast at range (or by aiming the spell) to do so remotely would require either sympathetic casting or if you're remote viewing it (like through a security camera), you have to spend a reach.<br /> <br /> As for practices, it'd probably be compelling or ruling for most things to do with computers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T01:04:46-07:00","id":882656,"title":"","content":"<u>Prime Questions</u>:<br /> <br /> Platonic Form, p.169 - What constitutes an &quot;action&quot; to use up mana? For example, if you summon a platonic wrench to help repair a car, would the entire extended repair roll use up a single mana or each roll per interval? Similarly, would a summoned sword consume a mana for an entire scene of combat, each hit or each attack regardless of whether it strikes anything?<br /> <br /> Can Platonic Form (or another Prime spell) be used to create applicable spellcasting Yantras? Would a platonic cup, wand, coin, mirror, dagger, etc. satisfy the Path and Order tool requirements? Can it be used to create effective platonic Sacrament Yantras? Could the Prime 2 spell As Above, So Below be used to further enhance such a Platonic Form Yantra?<br /> <br /> Can Platonic Form create something like a universal identification or security card or would it be considered too complicated an object? If not, could Prime accomplish such an effect with another spell or Practice?<br /> <br /> What level of Prime would be required, if any, to create more complex, inanimate objects like guns, computers or cars? Would it just be a Reach effect of Platonic Form?<br /> <br /> Supernal Vision, p. 166 - If a mage is not touching the person, place or object he wishes to examine, does he need to spend Reach to raise the range of spell to Sensory? If the spell is not inherently Sensory without Reach, can a mage aim and throw the spell, as per the rules on p.115? [This range question also applies to other common one dot Knowing and Unveiling spells from other Arcana such as Know Spirit, Interconnections, Analyze Life, etc.]<br /> <br /> Does Supernal Veil, p. 168, hide things only from supernal powers or from all detection? Does it ward only from magical/supernatural detection or also mundane perception?<br /> <br /> What Arcana and Practices, if any, are required to convert a physical object or sentient being to available mana that could be acquired and stored by a mage?<br /> <br /> What Prime Practices, if any, allow a mage to directly protect against the non-supernal powers of other supernaturals, akin to an expansion or extrapolation of Wards and Signs or Prime Armor? If such protection is possible, what penalties would be incurred against the attacker instead of a Withstand rating?<br /> <br /> Will Prime Mage Armor protect against effects of Disciplines, Blood Sorcery, Werewolf Gifts and Rights, etc.? If an effect/attack includes both physical and magical effects (e.g., firey hands), will Prime Armor still offer some protection?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Mind Questions</u>:<br /> <br /> Mind Shield, p. 160-61 - Why is Potency the primary factor? The defense is based in Clash of Wills, and Potency is only applicable to attempts at dispellation. Duration seems like it should be the primary factor.<br /> <br /> How is Mind 2 Psychic Domination with the Reach benefits that takes total control of the subject only a Ruling Practice? Wouldn't it be Patterning, or at the very least, Weaving? Don't the Reach benefits change the Practice of the spell?<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Spirit Question</u>:<br /> <br /> What Practice is required to fix / separate someone or something that has been Claimed by a spirit? Would such a spell require Spirit plus the addition of Life or Matter?<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Space Questions</u>:<br /> <br /> If a mage wants to cast a spell on a subject he is viewing through a scrying window, how many Reach for Range must he employ? Would he require one Reach to change from Touch to Sensory, and then another Reach to cast on a subject he\u2019s viewing remotely, or would one Reach be sufficient to directly affect the target through the window?<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Misc. Questions</u>:<br /> <br /> Are Rote and Praxis Experience costs a flat 1 Experience or 1 per level of the spell. For example, would an Adept-level rote costs 1 or 4 Experience points?<br /> <br /> Five Dot Arcana Attainment - Create Rote: Does a mage need to spend 1 Arcane Experience (in addition to the Willpower point and other requirements) to create the Rote or 1 Arcane Experience point per level of the Rote?<br /> <br /> Are there any guidelines or rules for creating an Abyssal environmental effect/tilt for a released Paradox other than the very brief passing mention on p. 116?<br /> <br /> Why does healing lethal damage require Life 4 and bashing only Life 3?<br /> <br /> Does possession or use of imbued or enhanced object count toward a mage's total spell control after the spell/attainment is relinquished?<br /> <br /> Do Hallows still provide the effective one free mana-equivalent when casting inside its area like as was the case in Mage 1e?<br /> <br /> Adamant Hand Merit. It was discussed in open development that the merit might be able to be used with Firearms. I just wanted to confirm the AH is indeed still just limited to Athletics, Brawl and Weaponry?<br /> <br /> Level 2 Life Attainment. During open development, it was mentioned that the level 2 Life Attainment provided an extended, robust and healthy life to the mage. Is this still the case, or was that removed in the final draft?<br /> <br /> Will there be rules in later supplements or blogs for creating non-spell legacy attainments such as those base on Merits.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Size/Area of Effect Questions</u>:<br /> <br /> On the Scale charts, Object Size (reference, p. 212) and Area of Effect do not correlate, with AoE consistently having a significantly larger volume (e.g., Size 10 car or Size 12 SUV to an AoE small or large warehouse). Is this intentional or an errata?<br /> <br /> Is the choice to use Size or AoE for a spell within the discretion of the PC at time of casting or is the factor inherent in the spell?<br /> <br /> For direct attack spells like Thunderbolt (or anything else such as blessing or repairing an object), if you're targeting a larger than human-sized object, for example a standard automobile, do you need to take casting penalties to increase Scale (size) to 10 in order to affect it (i.e., -10 roll penalty or a Reach and a -2 penalty, or for a Size 15 SUV, -20(!) or a Reach and -4) ?<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> What Prime Practice would allow the creation of edible and nutritious Tass?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 05-08-2016, 12:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T02:02:58-07:00","id":882684,"title":"","content":"The only thing im confused about are Temporal summoning and rewrite history. Both of these spells allows a mage to turn curtain supernatural back to humans temporarily. <br /> I thought mages can't do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T02:12:54-07:00","id":882691,"title":"","content":"Rote Question:<br /> <br /> If a master who created a Rote casts it from memory rather than a grimoire, does he get both the Mudra skill bonus AND rote quality on his spellcasting dice pool?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T02:41:26-07:00","id":882706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/880060-awakening-second-edition-faq-thread?p=882691#post882691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rote Question:<br /> <br /> If a master who created a Rote casts it from memory rather than a grimoire, does he get both the Mudra skill bonus AND rote quality on his spellcasting dice pool?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just read appropiate fragment:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MtAw 2E, p. 112</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Casting a Rote from a Grimoire rather than from memory, or <b>casting a Rote she designed hersel</b>f, gives the mage\u2019s spellcasting dice pool the rote quality.</div> </div> </div> </div>So yeah, from my reading you get both effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-05-2016, 05:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T03:32:28-07:00","id":882732,"title":"","content":"With Velocity Control the spell says that you can't target discrete components of a whole (The wheel on a truck) while that thing is in motion, why? What if I all I want is to slow the wheel so the truck jack-knifes off the road and I don't care about stopping the truck safely?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T03:43:02-07:00","id":882734,"title":"","content":"Are Yantras (and their + value) a vaid target for Creative Thaumaturgy Prime? Any suggestions on how to handle this? At first glance, it seems unbalanced to allow increasing Yantra bonuses by spells, as it can lead into Infinite Spiral (you raise Yantra Bonus, then use that Yantra to cast more powerful Yantra Bonus, then you use that Yantra to...). I like the concept, but can't pin down the numbers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T03:50:52-07:00","id":882741,"title":"","content":"What happens to things that got Ephemera-Shaped and then pulled out of Twilight? Do they retain their new shape? What if duration lapses when they are out of Twilight Phase?<br /> Am I right to assume that Dead Eyes and Ghost Gate both allow communication between Twilight Phase and Living Phase? Kind of like, Dead Eyes in Twilight allow you to perceive Living Phase as normal, and Ghost Gate in Twilight Phase allows you to tune things into Living Phase instead, etc?<br /> <br /> I really like handling Twiilght as a &quot;mode&quot;, instead of &quot;place&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T04:07:41-07:00","id":882753,"title":"","content":"Are Integrity and Integrity Equivalents subjects of Death's Arcanum purview, and thus vulnerable to Death Creative Thaumaturgy? It could be seen that way, as Integrity, Wisdom and other things were usually refereed to as &quot;soul's health&quot;, and &quot;soul&quot; falls under it.<br /> <br /> Is broken chair a corpse, but falling both under a Death and Matter, but functional chair just Matter? Can you look at a broken chair with Forensic Gaze just like you would at a dead body, to go into CSI Las Moros mode?<br /> <br /> [Yes, I'm making a Death Detective.]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 05-05-2016, 07:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T04:18:10-07:00","id":882758,"title":"","content":"For Chronicles that intend to mix Nameless and Order Characters, or newly Awakened apprentices, or whatever things..and wanting them to be XP-balanced, or want to know how much XP it takes to achieve &quot;full magery&quot; XP by XP, is this estimate correct:<br /> - Rote Skills being worth 2 XP (due to 3rd dot of Mystery Cult Initiation allowing to take them, and thus, making them equivalent of 2 dot merit)<br /> - High Speech being worth 1 XP<br /> - Order Status being worth 1 XP<br /> - Order Tools being worth ?? XP<br /> - Occult dot being worth 1 XP<br /> - 6 Rotes being worth 6 XP<br /> - [for newly Awakened], 1 Arcanum dot being worth 4 XP<br /> - [for non-Awakened] 1 Attribute dot being worth 5 XP<br /> Thus making &quot;Order Training&quot; worth 11 or 15 XP, and &quot;Awakened Template&quot; 20 XP?<br /> I understand why this is not in the book (it would distract from playing intended order protagonists, and if someone really cares, he can reverse engineer it because game is good and has everything transparent in cost department), just checking if my math is correct. And posting it for people who might have same question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T04:32:07-07:00","id":882765,"title":"","content":"Steadfast Condition (page 318) + Magic. Can you resolve it on a failed Spellcasting roll? It also lacks example sources (but that's something that every book does, so maybe it's intended).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">What Prime Practice would allow the creation of edible and nutritious Tass?</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><br /> Platonic form! Each bite should be considered a &quot;use of the item&quot;, and thus deplete Mana from it. more mana, more nom nom. </span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T04:35:39-07:00","id":882767,"title":"","content":"What is the interaction of Adamant Hand [Athletics] and Aimed Spells? Does the Aimed Spell roll (Gnosis+Athletics) &quot;trigger&quot; the Hand? Wooo benders wooo.<br /> Basically:<br /> I cast Aimed Spell. I roll Gnosis+Athletics to hit dude. It's Combat Use of Athletics skill. I can claim that as a Reflexive Order Tool Yantra worth +1? Or +Skill?<br /> Either way, does it use my one and only &quot;reflexive Yantra&quot;, or do I get two reflexive Yantras this way?<br /> [Please make it two reflexive Yantras so I can claim both it and Persona Yantra when playing magical samurai. Otherwise, it's not very attractive, as in combat you would rather grab biggest possible reflexive Yantra, not +1.]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 05-05-2016, 07:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T05:13:07-07:00","id":882787,"title":"","content":"<u>Mage Sight Questions</u><br /> <br /> 1. It is mentioned in the book that when an Acanthus looks at a knife with Mage Sight he sees the thousands of paths it could take, so does this mean he sees all of its uses? Or does this mean that he sees everyone that would use the knife or has used the knife? Or both? This is less of a mechanic question and more of a what did you mean with this one. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> 2. Are Dead Zones capable of being viewed with Mage Sight or are they just void of any symbols?<br /> <br /> Loving this book, it really shows all the hard work that was put into it and I like the style better than Mage 1E. Though I can tell things had to be cut short due to word count and that makes me a little sad, but otherwise I am definitely satisfied with this book and looking forward to the first addition, Signs of Sorcery!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T05:59:01-07:00","id":882802,"title":"","content":"Which books of 1st edition - if any - are invalidated by the new edition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/373-infernal-teddy","name":"Infernal Teddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar373_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T08:14:08-07:00","id":882880,"title":"","content":"What do ephemeral entities roll for a Clash of Wills? I might have just missed it, but it doesn't seem to be mentioned anywhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T08:36:15-07:00","id":882892,"title":"","content":"Hey DaveB, I have a humble request and some erratas:<br /> <br /> 1- Please, <u><b>remove the text from 2 Reach effect from Blasphemy spell and put in that place the mechanic of the Ansho</b></u> !!!! In other words, put this text in the 2 Reach place:<br /> <br /> <i><b><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">&quot;Every turn a mage remains in a Dead Zone, she loses a point of Mana. She cannot cast new spells at all. Her existing spells fade after a number of turns equal to her Gnosis. Spells targeting those within the Dead Zone have their Potencies halved each turn (round down) until they cease to exist.&quot;</span></b></i><br /> <br /> Another option is only saying that the rules from Ansho apply to the 2 Reach Blasphemy .<br /> <br /> <u><b>The actual 2 Reach effect from Blasphemy is absurdly bad and irrelevant (who needs a Lasting effect that isnt Lasting) and Prime need a usefull 5 Unmaking Spell</b></u>.<br /> <br /> Dont forget that the Ansho rules arent broken because a <u><b>simple 1 dot Prime effect can Dispel it and the Ansho is still a mistery, because it cant be dispelled.</b></u><br /> <br /> <br /> That said, some things that need a errata:<br /> <br /> 2- Eidolon spell is in essence the same thing that Golem spell, the only difference being that matter shapes inorganic matter and Prime shapes Mana/Tass.<br /> <br /> That said, I have conviction that <b><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Eidolon is a PATTERNING 4 dot Prime spell</span></b>, because the Golem is Patterning 4 dot Matter spell and the two spells are in essence the same thing: completely transform a target into something else that falls under the Arcanum\u2019s purview.<br /> <br /> 3- Plus, <b>like the Golem spell, Eidolon need the insertion of &quot;<i><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Add Death \u2022\u2022\u2022 or Spirit \u2022\u2022\u2022: Bind a ghost or spirit into the golem to serve as an animating intelligence</span></i></b><i>. The golem still uses its Retainer rating to determine dice pools, but the ephemeral being can use any of its powers, and the golem\u2019s \u201cfield</i>\u201d is whatever the entity is capable of.<b>&quot; </b>If Chaney dont have words for that just use<b> &quot;</b>Add Death \u2022\u2022\u2022 or Spirit \u2022\u2022\u2022: Bind a ghost or spirit into thegolem to serve as an animating intelligence.<b>&quot;</b><br /> <br /> 4- Again about Eidolon spell, the rule of <i><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">&quot;any mage may claim ownership of the tass simply by marking it with her Nimbus as per p.90. The new owner immediately gains any Retainer dots granted.&quot;</span></i> is absurd. <b><span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><u>We can agree that it need at least a Clash of Wills</u> </span></b><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">because it is inside in the spell control of the caster, no </span><b><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">?</span> </b>I think that is better remove this part from the spell because the mage can start a &quot;Nimbus Season&quot; and make the retainer Eidolon useless in combat:<br /> <img src=\"http://i713.photobucket.com/albums/ww131/Yellowcake_bucket/wabbit_season.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Thanks a lot, DaveB.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4272,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4272-sp4rt01","user":"Sp4rt01","date":". 05-05-2016, 11:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4272-sp4rt01","name":"Sp4rt01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T09:28:29-07:00","id":882920,"title":"","content":"I don't think I understand how the Nimbus Tilt works. It gives penalties and bonuses based on half of gnosis right? But who gets those? Me or the victim, and can I nitpick how those are distributed? Maybe I'm just bad at reading but I couldn't tell if the Nimbus Tilt would give the winning Nimbus's owner buffs and debuffs, or if the person who is affected by the tilt gets those bonuses and or penalties.<br /> <br /> I'm guessing if it is the latter the point of giving bonuses is that if you accidentally hit an ally they can get something out of it? Like debuffing strength but buffing occult would mean that allied mages would benefit but an attacking hired muscle would be screwed on the exchange?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T09:39:26-07:00","id":882930,"title":"","content":"Is the procedure for acquiring Rotes as following: request Grimoire with Order Status, read Grimoir, practice Rotes, pay XP for Rotes, return Grimoire?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T10:10:31-07:00","id":882964,"title":"","content":"I wanted to follow-up on some confusion concerning how to ascertain the base primary factor from this discussion:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/882233-2e-clarification-steps-up-the-primary-factor-when-spellcasting\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...n-spellcasting</a><br /> <br /> <br /> The text states, p.113,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All spells have a primary spell factor of either Potency or Duration. After penalties have been applied for the desired spell factors, the player may move the primary factor up its chart a number of steps equal to the character\u2019s rating in the spell\u2019s highest Arcanum minus one. For example, a Forces spell with a primary spell factor of Duration would last for 5 turns when cast by a mage with her Forces Arcanum rated at 3 and a \u20132 penalty to her casting roll. </div> </div> </div>Unless I'm wrong about the math, wouldn't it be far less confusing to simply state,<br /> <br /> &quot;A spell's base primary factor equals a mage's dots in the highest Arcana used in the spell, and each -2 dice penalty on the spellcasting roll increases it by one step on the applicable standard or advanced Factor chart?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 05-05-2016, 02:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T10:11:04-07:00","id":882967,"title":"","content":"If using the second dot of the Professional Training merit, which lets you select two Skills as Asset Skills in which you always have 9-again, does that 9-again also apply within the context of Rote spellcasting dicepools? I.e. if my Physicist character has Science as an Asset Skill and casts Shadow Sculpting as a Rote Spell, which has Science as one of the Rote Skill suggestions, does that mean she gets 9-again on the spellcasting dicepool?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T10:39:54-07:00","id":882991,"title":"","content":"Does High Speech count as one Yantra for the purposes of As Above, So Below?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T10:40:38-07:00","id":882992,"title":"","content":"Question: Does Mana spent reducing Paradox count as Mana spent on the spell for the purposes of the refund gained when scoring an Exceptional Success casting the spell?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T10:47:41-07:00","id":883002,"title":"","content":"This might have already been asked! Do dedicated items always have to be specific physical items? I can't quite tell whether the dedicated drumming example is centered on the rhythm or the drum. Can you use an Adamantine Hand style or Techne specialty as your dedicated tool?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T10:50:54-07:00","id":883007,"title":"","content":"Do mages have a more difficult time crossing the Gauntlet to the Shadow during the day like werewolves (W:tF 2e, p.101), or it makes no difference?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T10:53:20-07:00","id":883015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/880060-awakening-second-edition-faq-thread?p=882880#post882880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do ephemeral entities roll for a Clash of Wills? I might have just missed it, but it doesn't seem to be mentioned anywhere.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Influence + Rank","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T10:55:42-07:00","id":883020,"title":"","content":"On p. 113, I am rather confused about the example of increasing the duration of a spell. The example has a mage with Forces 3 and he prolongs it to 5 turns for a -2. So I think I have misunderstood how the whole mechanic works.<br /> <br /> I was under the impression that when you wanted to increase a spell's duration, you just took a penalty (-2, -4, -6, ect..), which was at the rank you wanted. For example, if you wanted it to last 3 turns you took a -4 penalty. Instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T11:12:29-07:00","id":883039,"title":"","content":"Not sure if this has been asked yet, but why are the summoning spells (Summon Ghost, Summon Spirit) Perfecting spells instead of Ruling? They're basically just Command X in a slightly different form, so why the change in Practice?<br /> <br /> Edit: Looks like it has. Call this a vote for this being answered, then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T11:33:17-07:00","id":883059,"title":"","content":"Can you witness your own Nimbus Flare, and willingly take the Nimbus Tilt on yourself? This is a serious question, as it would make certain mundane skill oriented characters pretty happy due to boosting their favorite skills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T11:39:13-07:00","id":883062,"title":"","content":"If you possess Universal Counterspell Attainment, does it make all 1 Dot Counterspell Attainments irrelevant, or do they provide some additional bonus to the mage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5973,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","user":"Prometheus","date":". 05-05-2016, 03:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T12:01:21-07:00","id":883082,"title":"","content":"You could very easily still have a higher rating in the other Arcana than you do in Prime.<br /> <br /> Example: County McCounterspell has Death 4, Prime 2, and Forces 1.<br /> <br /> Seer McExarchface casts a Spirit 3 spell at him. County McCounterspell has no Spirit, so uses Universal Counterspel to Clash with Gnosis + Prime<br /> Banisher McStillHasIntegrityDoofus casts a Forces 4 spell at him. County McCounterspell has Forces, but it's less than his Prime, so Clashes with Gnosis + Prime. Like a boss.<br /> Tremere McLiche casts a Death 3 spell at him. County McCounterspell Clashes with Gnosis + Death","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T12:05:28-07:00","id":883084,"title":"","content":"Also, Dave, I think I remember you mentioning on 4chan, while talking about side effects of not having a sympathetic name, that you could create a new (Lasting?) name by first adding the new one to the mage and only then removing the old one. Is this still a thing?<br /> <br /> And just for clarification, you can have only one Attainment per Arcanum, with the exception of 2 dot Mage Armor/Lesser Utility, if potentially deciding between multiple (possibly additional storyteller-made) Attainments, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5973,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","user":"Prometheus","date":". 05-05-2016, 03:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T12:23:13-07:00","id":883102,"title":"","content":"I'm still not understanding the active mage sign examples given for hiding effects. I think maybe my logic is broken, but it reads like this: <br /> <br /> A light based invisibility spell would hide you from mind sight but not life sight because life sight doesn't need photons? But mind sight does for some reason? It also doesn't mention forces sight, which might help clarify. <br /> <br /> The next example says that a mind-based invisibility (obfuscate) would protect against forces sight or time sight, but not mind sight (because they use the same power source). Did we maybe mean to say Forces sight in the first example? <br /> <br /> Otherwise, it reads like an invisibility effect can protect you except from effects that are different from it and also from effects that are the same as it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6014-anivair","name":"Anivair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6014_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T13:03:07-07:00","id":883140,"title":"","content":"Can the effects of regular Conditions (Inspired, Steadfast) affect spellcasting rolls, or can spellcasting only be affected by special Conditions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T13:05:02-07:00","id":883144,"title":"","content":"Are Aimed Spells subject to Withstanding? I am guessing yes but I'd like to make sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T13:16:44-07:00","id":883159,"title":"","content":"Does Death Sight clash with Obfuscate?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T13:52:24-07:00","id":883185,"title":"","content":"A few Spirit questions:<br /> <br /> Can Spirit 3 still awaken an object's sleeping spirit?<br /> <br /> It appears that may require Spirit 5 &quot;Birth Spirit&quot; to accomplish - creating a new spirit wholecloth - but effects like Coaxing the Spirits and Gremlins still presume that dormant spirits are the norm.<br /> <br /> We have a &quot;Rouse Spirit&quot; spell again, but its mechanical effect is very different. That spell does read as if there was material trimmed along the way, though (&quot;What slumbers can always be awoken. This spell can <i>also </i>rouse a hibernating spirit prematurely&quot; - Also in addition to what?)<br /> <br /> On a related note, is Birth Spirit a Lasting effect or does it have a Duration (like Mind 5 &quot;Psychic Genesis&quot; etc.) after which the spirit discorporates? Does its Potency affect anything about the spirit created?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T14:10:20-07:00","id":883195,"title":"","content":"I have Forces 4 and Prime 4. I imbue an item (say, a ring) with Forces 4's Levitate and I use the +1 reach option to allow free flight. I choose the &quot;persistent (always active)&quot; option when imbuing but do not increase duration factors of the spell.<br /> <br /> Am I correct in assuming that doing this gives you an effective Indefinite duration of Levitate without having to increase its duration to &quot;Indefinite&quot; via Reach and Spell Factors?<br /> <br /> When is Mana consumed by the <i>Ring of Levitation</i>? Every duration interval? Never? Only if the spell is dispelled and needs to be reactivated?<br /> <br /> <br /> If instead of a ring I wanted a flying broomstick (where the broom would be the only recipient of the spell and would carry the rider) would that still be an Imbued item or would it be an Enhanced item?<br /> <br /> <br /> Can Imbued/Enhanced items be smooshed together via Matter 3's Wonderful Machine?<br /> <br /> <br /> If I'm trying to create, say, a magical sword can I increase its damage bonus with Matter 3? What about adding properties like Armor Piercing or the one that grants bonus dice to the roll (accurate?)?<br /> <br /> If I exceed my free reach when imbuing an item when (if ever) is paradox rolled if a) the spell imbued is persistent or b) activated?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 05-05-2016, 05:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T14:41:50-07:00","id":883217,"title":"","content":"If you choose to go nameless order instead of pentacle or seers, at Character creation, do you get a free dot or dots of Mystery Cult Inniate, in place of the normal order benifits or do you have to buy the MCI dots with merit points and experience points?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T14:46:12-07:00","id":883220,"title":"","content":"A Mage feels bad about hiding their new life from loved ones. What is the easiest way to turn them sleepwalker without any serious drawbacks?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T14:51:36-07:00","id":883228,"title":"","content":"&lt;scrapped&gt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 05-06-2016, 09:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T14:53:46-07:00","id":883230,"title":"","content":"The Time and Space Arcana sections refer to Sympathy, and give two traits used by Sympathy- Connection and Sympathy -to determine their Withstand rating.<br /> <br /> The rightmost trait makes sense to me- the weaker the connection, the harder it is to work a spell through it, but would the Connection rating then be the equivalent of the Yantra dice bonus from using something with that level of Connection to the target?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T15:28:41-07:00","id":883250,"title":"","content":"A rather dumb question a guess.. I'm sorry.<br /> <br /> Edit to better speak my mind:<br /> If you always get a free Reach for the fact itself of having enough dots in the required Arcanum, how does that relate to the personal spell limit? Is it correct to say that <br /> <br /> a) you can always cast one more spell beyond the limit, because you can possibly use the free Reach you get for meeting the number of dots in an Arcanum?<br /> b) the second exceeding spell costs two Reaches, the third costs three Reaches, etc? (like: Gnosis 1 = Limit 1 spell; so the second spell costs one Reach, the third costs 2 Reaches; the fourth costs 3 Reaches and so on)<br /> <br /> <br /> Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11601,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11601-sbiricuda","user":"sbiricuda","date":". 05-06-2016, 07:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11601-sbiricuda","name":"sbiricuda","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T15:45:17-07:00","id":883262,"title":"","content":"Page 327<br /> <br /> Determine Yantras<br /> <br /> Characters may incorporate Yantras up to limit from Gnosis (p. XX). <br /> <br /> The infamous pXX strikes again <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T16:45:30-07:00","id":883295,"title":"","content":"So, in the 2e corebook a mage can only gain mana through sacrificing people the following ways:<br /> <br /> 1) Kill a small animal, gain 1 point of Mana.<br /> <br /> and<br /> <br /> 2) Kill a human being, get [Integrity] points of Mana.<br /> <br /> However, in the Sundered World Dark Era mages can sacrifice larger livestock for larger quantities of Mana. Goats and pigs and such are worth 2 points of Mana, and cattle are worth 5 points of Mana. Is this still true in the modern era, or is it specific to the pre-Sundering world?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T16:57:32-07:00","id":883304,"title":"","content":"Ignore, misread something and missed an important detail. Deleted incorrect text","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T17:06:51-07:00","id":883314,"title":"","content":"<b>Imbue Items is still kind of complicated. I think we need some clarification on how powerful the spell going into the imbue item can be. Specifically the line, &quot;</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">The mage can imbue an item with any spell she is capable<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">of casting. </span></span></span></span><br /> &quot;<br /> So this bit here... do imbue items have to contend with spellfactors and reach, or is this saying that, if after doing reach and spellfactors I can safely cast a spell with at least 1 die and no paradox dice it is imbueable, or do spellfactors and reach apply even after the spell is imbued. Like if a sleepwalker is using a magic gun that shoots bursts of kinetic energy to blast things out of the way, is it going to be single target, or can the sleepwalker apply the items reach from its arcana to blast something really large out of the way? If not, then is that something the imbuer has to account for, and decide going in if this gun can only blow small things away or if it can level entire buildings with a burst of kinetic energy?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T18:07:18-07:00","id":883352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/880060-awakening-second-edition-faq-thread?p=883314#post883314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Imbue Items is still kind of complicated. I think we need some clarification on how powerful the spell going into the imbue item can be. Specifically the line, &quot;</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">The mage can imbue an item with any spell she is capable<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">of casting. </span></span></span></span><br /> &quot;<br /> So this bit here... do imbue items have to contend with spellfactors and reach, or is this saying that, if after doing reach and spellfactors I can safely cast a spell with at least 1 die and no paradox dice it is imbueable, or do spellfactors and reach apply even after the spell is imbued. Like if a sleepwalker is using a magic gun that shoots bursts of kinetic energy to blast things out of the way, is it going to be single target, or can the sleepwalker apply the items reach from its arcana to blast something really large out of the way? If not, then is that something the imbuer has to account for, and decide going in if this gun can only blow small things away or if it can level entire buildings with a burst of kinetic energy?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm going to ask the same. How I see it: Imbuing an Item gives that item ability to cast that single spell using Spellcasting Pool equal to Arcanum + user's Gnosis. They set all the variables during the casting, *NOT*the imbuing. You don't preset the factors for the spell, they are set each time item is used.<br /> Think about it like this - Imbued Item is giving someone &quot;a licence&quot; to cast that spell, but you need to produce it on your own. It isn't a hung spell that you cast into it to unleash later.<br /> But some parts of the description are confusing, especially of the Attainment. Merit is very clear on what it does. There is dissonance between picture painted by merit and attainment, like they use two different systems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 05-06-2016, 09:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T19:06:39-07:00","id":883387,"title":"","content":"No to be that guy, but you all do remember that this is for an FAQ, right? Can we try not to clutter it up with stuff that should go in the Errata and corrections thread or answers to other poster's questions, like Dave asked us?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/880060-awakening-second-edition-faq-thread#post880060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) Please do not supply answers to other posters' questions, even if you think the answer's obvious..</div> </div> </div> </div>And to keep it on topic:<br /> <br /> Q. Can a mage use Sympathetic Yantras to target him or herself?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T21:05:37-07:00","id":883457,"title":"","content":"Why in the spell Possession do we have to spend mana to use our own mental attributes?<br /> Shouldnt this be the normal way? Using the physical of the host and mental of the posseser (is this a word?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11395-shaddar","name":"Shaddar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"338"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T01:15:07-07:00","id":883564,"title":"","content":"Would a mage flaring their nimbus be able to use it in place of a vampire lashing out with their predatory aura for the purposes of counteracting majesty?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T01:51:32-07:00","id":883586,"title":"","content":"Spell Potency<br /> On p. 113 under Potency, it sais Advanced Potency adds +2 to its Withstand ability; am I then right to assume that it does nothing to actually increase the potency of the spell, where other Advanced Factors actually affect the &quot;aspect&quot; they advance??","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T01:58:55-07:00","id":883593,"title":"","content":"Concerning Withstand I think something is missing: advice on when an improvised spell has this trait. For instance, in Vampire's Blood and Smoke, it was really helping when they said as a rule of the thumb: resistance was substracted from the dice pools when the number of successes were an important issue and was rolled a contested roll when a single success was enough. I have the distinct impression that this goes for Withstand as well: if a single success would do the trick we use Withstand, if the number of successes is important we won't, we would increase Potency instead.That might be worth mentioning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T03:28:35-07:00","id":883627,"title":"","content":"Are praxis meant to treat all tools used in them as dedicated like in the spoilers? or was that dropped?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T03:43:22-07:00","id":883629,"title":"","content":"So these are going to be specific questions on spells and examples from the core book... If the tone of the questions is a little &quot;powerplayer&quot; style, i apologize in advance but i play with a group that is really good at exploiting every last inch of power of any supernatural perk or ability, so to mantain balance in my game i have to ask in advance..<br /> <br /> 1) pag 130 death speel suppress life&quot;- if i am reading it right, does this spell allow a mage to &quot;put a living being to sleep&quot; for the duration? And its not even withstand? Like i can touch a guy on the street and &quot;kill him&quot; temporarily? and if so, how would it work against say a vampire since he is already dead? or a werewolf?<br /> <br /> 2) Does the spell ghost gate (same page) allow also a mage to just touch a subject and project him into the twilight as a ghost even if he is not sentient and doesn't want to? Again, i would allow withstand at least to save the poor average guy from finding himself suddenly in nightmare land. This is a similar question related to the space spell co location, where if i read it correctly a mage basically can touch someone and teleport him in the bathtub he was just sitting in an hour ago...<br /> <br /> 3) Does the spell telekinesis force 3 pag 144 allow a mage to just toss anyone against their will like they are objects? like a character magneto style just using his telekinesis to throw a bad guy across the room or simply lifting him in the air? shouldn't this also be withstand say for example with strenght (i think it was contested with a strenght roll the other edition..)<br /> <br /> 4) does the spell turn momentum forces 3 pag 145 basically allow a mage to dodge any attack incoming (not magical or supernatural)- since anything in our world needs momentum for hitting or damaging anything from a bullet to a punch to a knife? (granted that the mage has enough reaches and time to cast the spell)<br /> <br /> 5) general question about paradox (i know i look dumb but... maybe i am)<br /> If i understand correctly the concept of paradox in this edition (which by the way i love) if im in my sanctum or alone or i find myself on the street and no one is watching me, no human or sleeper in sight, throwing a lighting bolt or go back in time cause no paradox roll to occur at all?? granted i dont use reach etc... &lt;So as a general rule- no human looking=no paradox??<br /> <br /> side notes- apologize in advance for my english/ not my first language, and i wrote this while walking on the street- also, since im not used to read english anymore maybe that's the reason why i find some phrases in the book obscure or ambiguous..<br /> **really fucking good job guys, everyone from dave to all the developers of the book. U did great seriously, u produced a really nice and coherent work and a jewel of a game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4247,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","user":"Lasombra","date":". 05-06-2016, 06:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T04:26:50-07:00","id":883644,"title":"","content":"Q: if you're a virgin and turn 30 years old, to which Watchtower do you awaken?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T06:53:36-07:00","id":883711,"title":"","content":"Could we ask for an example statblock for an example Apprentice, &quot;Medium&quot;, and Master Mages?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T07:11:19-07:00","id":883728,"title":"","content":"How do we determine starting attributes / numina for a ghost / spirit / goetia familiar or being created using the relevant arcana? Right now I'm just running on they get the minimum value for their rank.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T07:45:27-07:00","id":883769,"title":"","content":"When you design Legacy Attainments, they are technically your Praxis spells burned into your Soul. Can you then use Attainments that, like the spells might have, use Arcana Attainments like Conditional Duration or Sympathetic Range? With the presumption that you would need to know the Arcana of those Attainments as prerequisites, of course.<br /> <br /> On that note, can you choose to not use the Reach effect(s) that you Legacy Attainments have available and/or can you swap it for a different Reach effect? I presume not, but I'd rather be certain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T07:56:11-07:00","id":883784,"title":"","content":"Many one dot knowing and unveiling spells simply enhance sensory perceptions (e.g., Analyze Life, Interconnections, Nightvision, Pierce Deception, Supernal Vision, The Outward and Inward Eye, etc.).<br /> <br /> When casting such spells, are the Sensory and/or Scale - Subjects/Area of Effect Factors already included as inherently part of the spell, or must penalties and/or Reach be used for the spell to be effective?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T08:08:22-07:00","id":883797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/880060-awakening-second-edition-faq-thread?p=883728#post883728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do we determine starting attributes / numina for a ghost / spirit / goetia familiar or being created using the relevant arcana? Right now I'm just running on they get the minimum value for their rank.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'd start with the maxium traits, but you arrive at the miniums when they trade them for something else, like trading Numena for Influence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T08:37:21-07:00","id":883810,"title":"","content":"Alright so I got a couple of questions for temporal sympathy.<br /> <br /> Firstly when you cast a spell thst effect someones past, you have target the person in the present current? So that does mean when your casting the spell the target's mage sight goes off letting them know they are being targeted right? <br /> <br /> Also for withstanding a spell cast on your past self, do you use your current resistance stat if spell has to target your present self? Or do you use the resistance stat of the past version of yourself? <br /> <br /> Lastly temporal sympathy needs a sympathy yantra to work. So does the target in the present work as a sympathy yantra for casting the spell or do you need something from the time desire you effect. Like a middleschool report card to effect them from back when they where in middle school?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T11:53:38-07:00","id":883945,"title":"","content":"Is there a minimum Retainer dot rating for a Sleepwalker or Proximus retainer?<br /> <br /> <br /> Do all Proximi Blessings default to a minimum of 5 hour(!) rituals to activate unless they expend a non-free Reach and incur a Paradox risk that cannot be contained, if successful will cancel the entire spell and will trigger the worse aspect of their Curse? They also cannot increase their Willpower dice pool with Yantras or by other means? Isn't this a little harsh?<br /> <br /> Can Proximi purchase supernatural merits available to humans from the CofD and other corebooks?<br /> <br /> Can Proximi share supernatural templates, e.g., a Proximus ghoul or wolf-blooded?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T15:02:45-07:00","id":884100,"title":"","content":"How does the Familiar condition interact with Anchor? Can a ghost familiar go where I or it wants or is it still bound by it's anchors? <br /> <br /> Does the familiar treat me or the thing it's fettered to as having the open condition or can it apply it with influence?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T15:10:11-07:00","id":884109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/880060-awakening-second-edition-faq-thread?p=883810#post883810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright so I got a couple of questions for temporal sympathy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't forget &quot;does a stick figure count as representational&quot;.<br /> I'm expecting that &quot;cast a spell through time&quot; means &quot;perform an action that effects history&quot; while &quot;casting a spell on the subject as it exists now&quot; means &quot;targeting this person at this time&quot;. With the last section about combining Sympathy types meaning &quot;targeting this person at this time, even if they aren't present&quot;<br /> <br /> Can Proximi pattern scour? And can oblations be performed just whenever?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T17:48:15-07:00","id":884190,"title":"","content":"At the bottom of the character sheet there are some mistakes:<br /> <br /> - Characters start with mana as per listed on the Gnosis chart and not mana=Wisdom<br /> - Who you distribute your dots amongst Arcana is incorrect on the character sheet<br /> - Favored Resistance Attribute can be Resolve/Stamina and Composure and doesn't depend on the character's Order<br /> - 10 points in Merits and not 7<br /> - Defense is the lowest between Wits and Dexterity + Athletics, Athletics was forgotten<br /> <br /> Plus, not enough space (imo) for rotes, some should had been made to note the Primary Spell Factors<br /> Nothing about Nimbus on the character sheet","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1851,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","user":"JPS","date":".  Erf, Sorry didn't see the new errata thread. This post should be there instead 05-06-2016, 08:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T17:50:27-07:00","id":884194,"title":"","content":"Can your dedicated tool also be your Order/Path tool ? If so, does it count as one Yantra (one tool) or two (since you're cumulating two beneficial effects into a single tool) ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T18:22:37-07:00","id":884221,"title":"","content":"How often is Dissonance rolled?<br /> <br /> The text (p.299) states it's just rolled after the scene in which a Sleeper witnesses obvious magic, with successes potentially slowly eroding the spell.<br /> <br /> What happens if the Sleeper is continually exposed to Supernal magic, such s being transformed into an animal or statue. How often does he get to roll to break down the spell.<br /> <br /> Also, since the dice pool is Integrity and Dissonance is Withstood by the Arcana dots in the spell, higher level spells are extremely resistant to Dissoance. Are there any bonuses to the Integrity roll and/or reductions in the Withstand rating for time or repeated or lengthy exposure to Sleepers?<br /> <br /> <br /> There's also some confusion concerning the spell factors and Reach of imbued items. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/882916-imbued-items\">See this discussion</a>.<br /> <br /> Could you offer a detailed example of the creation and use of an imbued item with various spell factors and multiple Reach?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 05-06-2016, 09:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T19:11:06-07:00","id":884250,"title":"","content":"How much time does it take to Concentrate on a spell as an Action Yantra ?<br /> How much time would it take to chant a High Speech incantation as an Action Yantra ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T19:23:07-07:00","id":884257,"title":"","content":"The Adamant Hand Merit says &quot;This Merit allows use of that Skill in combat as a reflexive Order tool Yantra, adding dice to <i>a</i> spell cast on subsequent <i>turns</i>, or to a spell cast reflexively in the same turn as the combat action.&quot; Do the bonus dice only apply to <i>one</i> spell cast on <i>a subsequent turn</i>, or do they apply to <i>all</i> spells cast on subsequent <i>turns</i>? (I assume the former). If the former, can I use the Skill multiple turns and save the bonuses up to use on multiple subsequent spells (for example, if I make a Brawl attack on the first and second turn, can I apply the bonus dice from one use to a spell I cast on the the third turn and the bonus dice from the other to use a spell I cast on the fourth turn)? If the latter, are the bonus dice cumulative? (I assume not).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T20:46:44-07:00","id":884322,"title":"","content":"So, I'm not sure on how to use Bind Spirit or it's equivalents to possess and possibly merge beings. If you are aiming to create a Possessed Condition linking a spirit and a given person, how exactly does that spell work? Do I need to cast Bind Spirit with an extra target penalty and match the potency against a Withstand trait for the person?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T22:38:29-07:00","id":884394,"title":"","content":"Something I'd like to know is how Mage Armor interacts with real armor. I know the old rules allowed them to stack but do they do the same now? 8/5 Riot Armour certainly sounds devastatingly powerful.<br /> <br /> Also I cant find any reference to bonus damage on spells like firearms have, I assume that is not a thing?\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1510-mysticjackal","name":"MysticJackal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1510_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T22:56:09-07:00","id":884399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MysticJackal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/880060-awakening-second-edition-faq-thread?p=884394#post884394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I'd like to know is how Mage Armor interacts with real armor. I know the old rules allowed them to stack but do they do the same now? 8/5 Riot Armour certainly sounds devastatingly powerful.<br /> <br /> Also I cant find any reference to bonus damage on spells like firearms have, I assume that is not a thing?\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I'm pretty sure 1e mage armor could Not stack with mundane armor. I don't see why that would change now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T23:43:58-07:00","id":884419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022 If the object can be used as a tool, add +1 equipment bonus. Each action using the tass as a tool, however, uses up 1 point of its Mana as the profane matter of the Fallen World corrupts the purity of the Form. </div> </div> </div><s>Does this mean ALL of Platonic Form's mana gets used up when it's used as an equipment, or only the mana put into it for that option?<br /> Doing the Green Lantern thing is my favourite thing to do with Prime, and I've got a player who wants to summon swords, so I'm probably going to allow Platonic Forms to stick around, with only equipment bonus mana being spent on use, but an official ruling would still be good.</s><br /> I read that wrong, you're spending Potency, not mana, so even if you have 5 potency but 1 mana, you have one swing. Man, that power got really disappointing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":2998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","user":"Aspel","date":". 05-07-2016, 03:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T00:33:07-07:00","id":884439,"title":"","content":"What would you say to the thought that Spirit is too narrowly constrained when compared to Death?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T00:52:53-07:00","id":884446,"title":"","content":"Did a ctrl+f through the thread so I don't think it's been raised yet.<br /> <br /> Fate 1, Quantum Flux, the first paragraph removes all penalties to a subject's actions. Does this include Spellcasting actions? The second paragraph talks about a <i>bonus</i> and how the <i>bonus</i> doesn't apply to spellcasting. Should the limitation applied to the <i>bonus</i> also be applied to the <i>penalty negation</i> aspect?<br /> <br /> Fate 2, Shifting the Odds, how does the primary factor of Duration impact the spell? Potency determines the number of uses of the gained merits, the default use specifies within the next 24 hours and the Reach effect reduces the time to the next 1 hour. What does Duration do and why does increasing it help?<br /> <br /> Fate 2, Warding Gesture, would this have any effect on protecting someonme against being tricked into signing a Changeling Contract or a deal with a Demon? What would be the dice pool used by Changelings or Demons as neither of those abilities have an equivalent to Arcanum to Clash of Wills?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","user":"Scutarii","date":". 05-07-2016, 04:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T03:48:42-07:00","id":884514,"title":"","content":"Does Supress Life actually send the subject into a death-like coma a la Romeo and Juliet as it did in 1e, or, since it's a Veiling effect, does it just make them appear clinically dead while they're free to get up, walk around, eat, get into fights, or whatever they like? The spell's description could go either way, depending on how you interpret it.<br /> <br /> I remember hearing that Fate-based Target Exemption was a spell now (with the Fate 2 Attainment being Conditional Duration). Did I miss it in the spell list? If not, which dot-level should it be? The conjunctional component of Scrying in Space implies still Fate 2, but I'm not sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1909,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","user":"Juhn","date":". 05-07-2016, 07:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T04:40:37-07:00","id":884546,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The use of the term &quot;Doors&quot; borrows from the same terminology used in the Social Manipulation rules. That taken into mind -<br /> <br /> Do merits, spells and other effects that also affect Doors (resisting, opening and/or closing them) like &quot;Sympathetic&quot; also apply here? <br /> Does the proper use of Status (&quot;I am your superior so you should yield&quot;) affect these dice rolls? <br /> Would it be possible for a Silver Ladder to use the Lex Magica merit to affect the contest, or a Seer with the Unity prelacy? <br /> How is it possible to open a Door (or multiple Doors) through negotiations if the impression is not anything less than perfect?<br /> Since the attacks are described as assaults on the mind, spirit and body, does the Merit &quot;Indomitable&quot; apply? Iron Will?<br /> <br /> If, in fact, the Duel Arcane is not actually Social Maneuvering, wouldn't it clear up any misconceptions or misassumptions to change the name from &quot;Doors&quot; to something else that would achieve the same results?</span></span> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Considering that the Duel is supposed to be the first-course of action / preferred way of settling disputes amongst Mages, the word-count seems very low (much less than 1e) and the lack of structure can lead someone to believe that outside of the mechanical guidelines here, that &quot;anything goes&quot;. Is it expected that the rules governing 2E Duel Arcane should default to the material in Tome of the Mysteries (not one of the six books recommended) and 1st edition or will there be an expansion/reiteration of the Code Duello in the next or a future supplement? </span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1605-thatguy","name":"ThatGuy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T05:53:14-07:00","id":884567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Juhn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/880060-awakening-second-edition-faq-thread?p=884514#post884514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember hearing that Fate-based Target Exemption was a spell now (with the Fate 2 Attainment being Conditional Duration). Did I miss it in the spell list? If not, which dot-level should it be? The conjunctional component of Scrying in Space implies still Fate 2, but I'm not sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fate 2, Warding Gesture, pg.136, read the second paragraph of the spell.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T09:09:18-07:00","id":884674,"title":"","content":"1) Would a mage using a grimoire to ritually cast a healing spell with an advanced duration use their base ritual casting time or the modified ritual cast time to determine how often the healing recurs?<br /> <br /> 2) Maybe this should be in the errata thread instead, but I'm not sure if it's an actual mistake or just a difference of interpretation between myself and the developers. It feels like the effects of Control Gravity and Gravity Supremacy have been swapped. All of the other example &quot;Control&quot; spells in the Forces Arcanum strengthen or weaken the force in question, which is what Gravity Supremacy does. Control Gravity lets the mage radically change the direction of gravity, which feels more like a weaving spell like Turn Momentum.<br /> <br /> Edit: There is a tacked on section at the very end of Gravity Supremacy talking about making objects fall in other directions, although that doesn't really fit with the rest of the spell description. It still feels like strengthening/weakening gravity should be a Forces 2 Ruling effect while changing gravity's direction should require Weaving (Forces 3).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3755,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","user":"Jaerys","date":". 05-07-2016, 12:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","name":"Jaerys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T09:30:31-07:00","id":884687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ThatGuy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/880060-awakening-second-edition-faq-thread?p=884546#post884546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The use of the term &quot;Doors&quot; borrows from the same terminology used in the Social Manipulation rules. That taken into mind -<br /> <br /> Do merits, spells and other effects that also affect Doors (resisting, opening and/or closing them) like &quot;Sympathetic&quot; also apply here?<br /> Does the proper use of Status (&quot;I am your superior so you should yield&quot;) affect these dice rolls?<br /> Would it be possible for a Silver Ladder to use the Lex Magica merit to affect the contest, or a Seer with the Unity prelacy?<br /> How is it possible to open a Door (or multiple Doors) through negotiations if the impression is not anything less than perfect?<br /> Since the attacks are described as assaults on the mind, spirit and body, does the Merit &quot;Indomitable&quot; apply? Iron Will?<br /> <br /> If, in fact, the Duel Arcane is not actually Social Maneuvering, wouldn't it clear up any misconceptions or misassumptions to change the name from &quot;Doors&quot; to something else that would achieve the same results?</span></span> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Considering that the Duel is supposed to be the first-course of action / preferred way of settling disputes amongst Mages, the word-count seems very low (much less than 1e) and the lack of structure can lead someone to believe that outside of the mechanical guidelines here, that &quot;anything goes&quot;. Is it expected that the rules governing 2E Duel Arcane should default to the material in Tome of the Mysteries (not one of the six books recommended) and 1st edition or will there be an expansion/reiteration of the Code Duello in the next or a future supplement? </span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Seconded. Change it to &quot;Seals&quot; or whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T09:30:31-07:00","id":884688,"title":"","content":"doublepost because my mouse sucks <br /> <br /> Ok, using the double post for something useful.<br /> <br /> Game mentions at many places that Spells inflict conditions and tilts. Creative Thaumaturgy tells you to make Spells work off the Condition system. However, amost no spell actually imposes a Condition, especially in Mind Magic. Should effects of such spells considered Conditions for things like Pattern Restoration?<br /> ...Yes, basically I'm asking &quot;If someone turns me into a Frog, should I be able to Cleanse that FrogForm Tilt by spending Mana, and if someone Psychic Dominates me to suicide, can I cleanse the Psychic Domination with 3 Mana.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 05-07-2016, 02:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T11:47:38-07:00","id":884790,"title":"","content":"When determining which objects can be path tools, must the object be made entirely of the selected material? ex obrimos using solid gold cups vs plated cups","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5296-xeliffo","name":"xeliffo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T13:56:36-07:00","id":884884,"title":"","content":"Have you had any thoughts on how to handle Legacy conversions?<br /> <br /> I know publishing another book of Legacies would be a waste of everyone's time and money, but I want it so bad anyway. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T17:50:41-07:00","id":885038,"title":"","content":"Items made of Ephemera pulled into physical realm...interact with Arcana how exactly? Imagine that I shape ephemeral matter into a physical object, and then pull it out of Twilight. Do I interact with it using Matter? What if I reshape some Ephemera into a body, and then pull it out of Twiilght? Is it a valid target for Quicken Corpse?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T18:04:26-07:00","id":885050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/880060-awakening-second-edition-faq-thread?p=884884#post884884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you had any thoughts on how to handle Legacy conversions?<br /> <br /> I know publishing another book of Legacies would be a waste of everyone's time and money, but I want it so bad anyway. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm having a hell of a time converting the Sphinx over (their First Attainment in 1e (Interconnections at 5 successes) is now Interconnections plus like four Reaches, for one thing, and I have <i>no</i> idea how to handle their Third Attainment), so I'm curious about this as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T18:08:06-07:00","id":885055,"title":"","content":"I might as well repost this here just in case.<br /> <br /> My interpretation of the Legacy Attainments rule is that 1) Legacy Attainments need to spend one Reach in order to be instant, and 2) when you design a Legacy Attainment, you have to assign its Reach, and Mages can't decide how their Attainments' Reach is spent. Is this correct?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T19:22:43-07:00","id":885092,"title":"","content":"Questions about Forces 5 Earthquake and similar Forces and structure damage spells:<br /> <br /> 1. Since buildings within the area of effect are stationary, does the Forces 2 Attainment Precise Force apply and targets within the area have two less Durability and suffer two additional Structure in damage?<br /> <br /> 2. If additional and/or Advanced Duration are applied to the spell, is damage continuously accrued, and if so, is it each turn or every Gnosis Ritual Level interval?<br /> <br /> 3. Does the Forces 4 Attainment Environmental Immunity protect the mage from the effects of the earthquake?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 05-08-2016, 01:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T22:03:49-07:00","id":885154,"title":"","content":"Page 125 states that instant healing spells are always Perfecting or Patterning spells, and Ruling can increase a subject's healing time.<br /> <br /> Why then is Purge Illness only a Life 2 Shielding spell and.capable of curing life-threatening diseases without additional Reach? The spell is not offering protection from a phenomena (i.e., disease), but rather bolstering or transforming the subject.<br /> <br /> Regardless of Practice for Purge Illness, is it automatically lasting like Knit and Mend, or is Duration a necessary factor, particularly if the disease is only mitigated and not cured?<br /> <br /> <br /> Life 1 Cleanse the Body only permits a single Potency bonus to one roll to reduce the ongoing damage from a toxin or poison (p. 148, 225). What Practice would be necessary to instantly cure a subject of lethal poisoning, Perfecting, Patterning or something else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 05-08-2016, 01:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T22:17:56-07:00","id":885162,"title":"","content":"Quicken Corpse (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <b>Practice: </b>Weaving<br /> <b>Primary Factor: </b>Duration<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills: </b>Medicine, Crafts, Persuasion<br /> <br /> The caster can animate a corpse, creating a loyal zombie servant. A zombie ... with a <span style=\"color:#800080\"><u><b>\u201cfield\u201d relating to the mage\u2019s commands</b></u></span>. Zombies have as much Health as the living creature their corpse came from had, but suffer damage as though they are under the effects of Death Mage Armor.<br /> <br /> Question: by &quot;fields&quot; do you mean skills ? and how many ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1851,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","user":"JPS","date":". 05-08-2016, 11:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T22:30:17-07:00","id":885173,"title":"","content":"State Change (Matter \u2022\u2022\u2022) <br /> <br /> Would it be possible, using a reach, to turn a gaz around someone's head int solid state thus chocking him to death ?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T00:09:23-07:00","id":885222,"title":"","content":"&quot;These beings, the Acamoth and Gulmoth, use similar rules to other ephemeral entities. Acamoth are treated as Goetia, while Gulmoth are treated as spirits.&quot; Page 252, Abyssal Entities.<br /> <br /> Is it only a mechanical thing, or does Spirit affect gulmoth like a spirit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T03:35:06-07:00","id":885277,"title":"","content":"How does Withstanding work against Legacy Attainments for spells that would normally be Withstood?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T03:55:26-07:00","id":885281,"title":"","content":"A simple one: does casting a spell immediately specifically an instant action? If not, how exactly does it work?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T05:59:49-07:00","id":885321,"title":"","content":"Not sure if this is a typo or not, but on p.92, where it discusses concealment from active mage sight, it gives an example of using a Forces spell to hide from Mind sight (perception of thinking beings), but says said spell could be pierced by Life sight (perception of living beings)? Is this a typo, or is there some logic to this that I'm missing? How could mere physical invisibility conceal someone from either of these effects?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T06:58:50-07:00","id":885344,"title":"","content":"I actually really like how you guys handled the Acanthus, implementing the Fool and Wheel of Fortune Tarot cards really adds to the identity. I remember the Fool being in 1e, but if all the Paths are now composed of 2 Tarot Cards, I'm wondering if that would be part of a template. You know, to help fleshout your &quot;homebrew&quot; path, choose 2 Major Arcana in addition to, well, major arcana, to help flesh out the cultural identity of said-path. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T08:53:39-07:00","id":885400,"title":"","content":"What happens to a Gulmoth that loses all Corpus?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T08:56:26-07:00","id":885402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tambov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/880060-awakening-second-edition-faq-thread?p=880941#post880941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\