:[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T11:24:33-07:00","id":886489,"title":"","content":"What action, if any, and what range, if any, can be used ot pass off a spell for a Sleepwalker to hold?<br /> <br /> E.g.: I have made an agreement with a Sleepwalker two days ago to hold a spell. I then cast a spell and need to pass it off to them to free up some reach for the critical life saving spell I need <i>right now</i>. Can I now activate the agreement we made and pass the spell on? Or would I need to touch the Sleepwalker or only make the deal <i>after</i> the spell is cast, etc.?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T12:24:40-07:00","id":886548,"title":"","content":"Why is Scrying a Ruling effect? It's a sensory expansion spell similar to post cognition isn't it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T15:47:52-07:00","id":886692,"title":"","content":"When using a Dedicated Magic Tool, does it count as a single Yantra or two Yantras to mitigate 2 Paradox and gain a +1 to the spell's dice pool?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6716-seulja","name":"Seulja","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T17:09:09-07:00","id":886763,"title":"","content":"Let me just say, I love the idea of the Duel Arcane, but I'm completely at a loss as to how it's supposed to work mechanically. I'm casting spells to open doors, I get that, and I have to use spell factors and what not as normal. I can't use more Reach than I get from my Arcana.<br /> <br /> ...how exactly do I open doors, though?<br /> <br /> I mean, I get the impression that its a Wizard's Duel, and I'm doing things like turning my opponent into a Mouse (Life), Turning His Mind to the Inevitability of his Defeat (Mind), or Poisoning his Imago so he can't Cast (Prime), and similar things sort of like that? Should I be guessing what arcana level would be required for the spell, and calculating how much Reach I need for that purposes, and then using it to get things like Duration and Sensory and what not? What is the Potency of the spells used for?? How do I know if I actually opened a door or not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/728-crownedsun","name":"CrownedSun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar728_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"217"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T17:19:22-07:00","id":886772,"title":"","content":"scrapped wrong thread","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 05-09-2016, 08:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T23:57:01-07:00","id":887024,"title":"","content":"If an effect would occur which does not create or destroy something per the unmaking/making practices, but would automatically kill an individual (such as the redirecting of the flow of blood in the body via forces or life) would it be withstood, be considered a damaging spell, or would it simply be raised to an unmaking spell because the end results in the automatic death of the individual?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T07:44:26-07:00","id":887151,"title":"","content":"Why is Earthquake an unmaking spell? What are you unmaking?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6014-anivair","name":"Anivair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6014_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T07:55:10-07:00","id":887163,"title":"","content":"Can you used previously scribed sigils and tattoos for the Runes Yantra, or do they need to be created fresh with each spell?<br /> <br /> Edit: Can switching the primary spell factor cause it to be something other than Duration or Potency, or is it always one of those two options?<br /> <br /> Edit 2: Teamwork casting questions:<br /> <br /> 1) do secondary casters need to try to match the spell factors of the leader, or is it just rolling their whole given pool to add bonus dice? If the former, why are the rules for having some but not all the Arcana needed so harsh? Gnosis - 3 - spell factors is extremely gnarly, to the point I question involving them in the first place. If the latter, how does Paradox ever come up for secondary casters? <br /> <br /> 2) can secondary casters benefit from their own Yantras? <br /> <br /> 3) If you have casters of different Gnosis, can the higher Gnosis casters get the bonus dice for extra time while their counterparts reach their base time? <br /> <br /> Basically I have no idea how teamwork casting is supposed to work, I suppose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":451,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","user":"Kirby Jerusalem","date":". 05-10-2016, 12:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T09:13:31-07:00","id":887229,"title":"","content":"Would the abilities of other supernaturals and spells cast on them stack? For example a vampire has accelerate cast on him and uses celarity. Would the vampire multiple the celarity speed, add the two multiplayers together, or just use the better if the two?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10820,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","user":"Blakemikizuki","date":". 05-10-2016, 12:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T10:08:11-07:00","id":887268,"title":"","content":"Wrong thread","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T10:46:11-07:00","id":887294,"title":"","content":"Why did you choose to give Death Mage Armor extra functions but not the Spirit Mage Armor which has most of the same mechanics? And why Did you limit these to working only a couple rounds when the other mage armors lasts a whole scene?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T10:50:10-07:00","id":887295,"title":"","content":"This has probably been asked before, but why is Temporal Stutter's primary factor Potency? Potency doesn't seem to <i>do</i> anything for the spell, whereas Duration seems to be the primary way to scale the effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T12:03:44-07:00","id":887367,"title":"","content":"Does the &quot;+1 die of Paradox per spell you've cast this scene that also risk Paradox&quot; apply an additional die to spells that already risk Paradox (either from overReaching, or from casting an obvious spell around Sleeper witnesses), like it worked in 1e (where it applied to further Vulgar or Improbable castings) or to <i>every</i> other spell you cast that scene? In the latter case it feels like casting a spell that risks Paradox effectively kills your ability to use your Arcana for the rest of the scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T12:13:14-07:00","id":887374,"title":"","content":"Lasting spells have effects which linger on after a spell has already run its course, but do those effects still suffer from successes on Dissonance rolls?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T14:26:46-07:00","id":887492,"title":"","content":"Okay so. If you have a character with Gnosis 10 and like 10 Strength, not modified by spells, all bought with experiences.<br /> You're out pumping iron with cars and asking the Sleepers if they even lift bro.<br /> <br /> Other than pissing off the local Guardians, does this effect anything?<br /> Do the Sleepers start to have seizures over how Supernal your strength is?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T15:13:58-07:00","id":887539,"title":"","content":"So, question regarding the Adamant Hand Merit and Active Mage Sight:<br /> Active Mage sight states:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While a character is using Active Mage Sight, she suffers a \u20132 modifier to all rolls unrelated to using or perceiving magic. </div> </div> </div> And then focused Mage sight increases this to a -3.<br /> <br /> Adamant Hand allows combat techniques (I.e. actions that involve Athletics, Brawl and/or Melee, including derived actions such a dodges) to count as Order Yantras. Would this allow an Arrow to use these actions without penalty while using active Mage sight, without facing a penalty, considering that they are part of &quot;using magic&quot; for the Arrow?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T16:10:01-07:00","id":887589,"title":"","content":"Quantum Flux again. Does it ignore penalties caused by supernatural means such as a penalty to noticing signs of passage from a Vampire using Obfuscate? Or would that be a Clash of Wills (which seems odd as they don't directly oppose).<br /> <br /> Do the <i>Successive Attempts</i> rules apply to spellcasting? I.e.: outside the heat of the moment with a Yantra for 3 dice, gnosis+arcana for 4 dice you take 6 spell factors for -12 leaving you with -5 dice (maximum allowable after accounting for Yantras). Spend a reach to instant cast plus any other reach (e.g.: a rote). You can just keep trying, spending a few seconds of intense concentration until the chance die are in your favour?<br /> <br /> Would Quantum Flux counter the dice pool penalties for <i>Successive Attempts</i> done in the heat of the moment?<br /> <br /> Would Quantum Flux counter the dice pool penalties for resistance attributes or defences?<br /> <br /> Would Quantum Flux counter dice penalties for targeting body parts in combat?<br /> <br /> Would Reach options allow for this even if the basic version of the spell doesn't?<br /> <br /> I assume it can't and never could apply to spellcasting rolls, no matter how much reach you have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","user":"Scutarii","date":". 05-10-2016, 07:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T16:22:46-07:00","id":887597,"title":"","content":"I love the book so far. I've always enjoyed using magical items in Mage, but they often seem to be a source of rules complications. Here are some issues I found when studying these merits in depth.<br /> <br /> <b>Some questions about the Artifact and Enhanced Item merits:</b><br /> <br /> There are a number of statements that imply that an Artifact casts spells on its own:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Artifact can also use its Mana as part of its own activation.<br /> <br /> Every Artifact will use its effects under different circumstances, determined when you create the Artifact.<br /> <br /> For example, an Artifact might cast its effect the moment it is first seen by human eyes, or whenever it\u2019s dropped on the ground. </div> </div> </div>If an artifact activates upon being dropped on the ground, then there is no user wielding it, so the artifact must be generating a spell effect independent of a user. The same applies for an artifact that is sitting out and is seen by someone from a distance. Is this interpretation correct? This raises a number of questions. Is the spell a reflexive action? If not, how long does it take for the spell to cast? If the trigger happens during a combat situation, where in the initiative does the spell occur?<br /> <br /> If an artifact is capable of multiple spell effects, does each one have a separate trigger? If they share a trigger, what is the timing of the spells with respect to the previous paragraph?<br /> <br /> Do artifacts regenerate their own mana naturally? Do they require the Channel Mana spell (Prime 3, pg. 168) to be recharged? Can an awakened user recharge it as per the rules under Imbued Item?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Artifacts cannot Reach beyond the \u201cfree\u201d Reach for their Arcana ratings on their own. </div> </div> </div>Is there a way an artifact can use a specific implementation of a spell using reach effects by default? How would this be represented by the merit?<br /> <br /> If an artifact's gnosis is higher than its user, can a ritual spell be cast using the artifact's gnosis for the timing?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>And some questions related to Enhanced Item:</b><br /> <br /> The description says that the item is enhanced with spells of persistent duration. Could this be a lasting effect instead, or are enhanced items inherently vulnerable to being dispelled? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A dot can provide +1 to the item\u2019s bonus as a tool </div> </div> </div>Can this apply to a weapon's damage? What spell can be used to replicate this effect? Alter Integrity (Matter 3, pg. 156) can be used to modify durability and structure, but not an equipment bonus.<br /> <br /> Why can Enhanced Item be combined with Imbued Item, but not with Artifact? Are artifacts normally immune to spells which modify their physical properties? (Word of Unmaking (Prime 5, pg. 171) says that the spell cannot be used to destroy Artifacts, although Annihilate Matter (Matter 5, pg. 158) can explicitly target magical objects using reach. Other spells (Find the Balance, Shaping, Aegis, Nigredo and Albedo, etc.) give no restriction.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1589-avatar","name":"Avatar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1589_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T18:54:56-07:00","id":887740,"title":"","content":"On pg. 68, it says, &quot;Each Mystery solved increases the Gnosis of the cabal as a whole, which makes all the members better-equipped to pursue deeper Mysteries&quot;, and this is seemingly never referred to again. Am I missing some effect of Gnosis somewhere or reading this wrong?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>A Green Sun Destrier</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/77-kongurous","name":"kongurous","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar77_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"417"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T20:53:25-07:00","id":887814,"title":"","content":"What does the &quot;Add fate <b>\u2022</b>&quot; effect on Dispel Magic... uhh... do?<br /> <br /> (for reference: The mage may suppress the subject spell selectively, for a number of subjects equal to Dispel Magic\u2019s Scale factor.)<br /> <br /> Nearest I can tell, the word &quot;selectively&quot; seems to be the only thing that isn't already possible without adding Fate 1, but what does it mean to suppress a spell selectively?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T04:08:46-07:00","id":888035,"title":"","content":"Potent Resonance Merit: Can you fall prey to your own Nimbus Tilt by scrutinizing your own work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T10:29:45-07:00","id":888343,"title":"","content":"Are the the Rank, Attribute, and Numena increases from the +2 Reach effect of Bolster Spirit Lasting?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T11:22:45-07:00","id":888388,"title":"","content":"Another crossover question!<br /> Does the unraveling practice do lethal/aggravated damage to Vampires, or does it get downgraded to bashing/lethal (respectively)? Or does it depend on the spell and how the damage is done?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T11:34:20-07:00","id":888405,"title":"","content":"Does the Quiescence erase the Sleeper's memory after the Apocalypse ends, or does the Sleeper remember, and do the Sleepers still cause Paradox when the spell is active?<br /> <br /> Also, Does the Apocalypse spell require you to spend 1 Reach for each Arcanum you add, or do you need to use only one Reach no matter how many Arcana you employ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5973,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","user":"Prometheus","date":". 05-11-2016, 03:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T14:17:47-07:00","id":888550,"title":"","content":"When you use Hung Spell, does the target of the spell being delayed have to be present at the time of the casting? For example, can I hang a fraying attack spell and then later trigger it to be cast on an enemy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T19:22:20-07:00","id":888764,"title":"","content":"The <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/paradoxical/\" target=\"_blank\">Paradox spoilers</a> indicated that the book would contain one sample Paradox Condition per Arcanum. <br /> <br /> Did they get cut for space in the final draft, or do the three Abyssal Conditions represent a change of game design and intent?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T20:16:28-07:00","id":888799,"title":"","content":"Shifting the Odds (Fate 2) is Potency Primary and uses Potency to determine temporary Merit dots for the alternative effect, as well as the number of uses the caster gets of that Merit. It also takes up to 24 hours to work, or up to 1 hour with Reach. Does it need to have a 1 or 24 hour duration to guarantee success? If you choose Merit dots, do they expire when the duration ends, or only after [Potency] uses? Would there be any issue with a Creative Thaumaturgy variant which had Duration Primary (to better spread out Merit uses, assuming they do expire when the spell does, or if you're only using the 'narrative' functionality)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4855-eggs-maledict","name":"Eggs Maledict","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T22:26:23-07:00","id":888845,"title":"","content":"Page 184, Shape Spirit. For each potency I can exact several effects, including &quot;<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">&quot; <span style=\"color:#000000\">Redistribute the spirit\u2019s Attribute dots.&quot; Is this meant to mean that all the dots can be shifted at once, or that it is on a one for one basis like with bolster spirit, as either could make sense from different angles.<br /> <br /> Additionally, what attributes would Birth spirit bring a spirit, 1/1/1 or would it be their maximum dots for rank 1 or rank 2 respectively.<br /> <br /> I also get the impression that bolster spirit, shape spirit, and birth spirit are all treated as different spells independant of each other. In first edition the create spirit spell let you set the dots of attributes and abilities as you spent successes on the ritual casting.<br /> <br /> What I'm guessing <i>now </i>is that if I want to create a powerful spirit with one single spell, I need to <i>combine</i> Birth Spirit or Shape Spirit with Bolster Spirit as a combination, and then the dots the rank 1-2 spirit starts with from the birth will be augmented by Bolster spirit with this combination spell?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: I can't tell if this has been asked yet but it sounds super important---How does Reach behave with combined spells? Does each of the combined spells get its own reach pool or is the reach for the spell with the most arcana dots spent between all the spells collectively and individually? Like a master spell combined with an apprentice spell means that both spells only have the 1 reach to spend between either of them?</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","user":"Scarlet Witch","date":". 05-12-2016, 01:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T00:32:09-07:00","id":888919,"title":"","content":"Assume the following: Police interrupt Supernal Summoning, shoot Supernal Entity with guns.<br /> <br /> What happens (beyond dissonance)? Does the Supernal Being apply Defence? What if Supernal Being has Time 2?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T03:28:38-07:00","id":888995,"title":"","content":"Can you make a Prime Legacy Attainment out of a Death Arcanum Attainment? I saw the Attainments question already asked concerning Mage Shield, but i was thinking specifically about &quot;Death: Inviolate Soul.&quot; <br /> <br /> [I'm also wondering why all the Soul manipulation falls under Death Purview. I mean, it is said that Souls are something elusive, requiring various Arcana to the Mastery level to be made, if at all. In fact, it could be said that as a Mage, each Path defines and changes that soul, shaping it with the particular Supernal Realm it Awakened into. So... wouldn't that Inviolate Soul be something of a &quot;communal&quot; attainment just like Mage Shield?]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T07:58:05-07:00","id":889117,"title":"","content":"I've got a question about Attainment spell factors:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When required, the Attainment is also considered to have acquired additional spell factors that would incur a penalty (if cast as a spell) equal to the Attainment\u2019s lowest prerequisite Arcanum (rounded down). </div> </div> </div>How does this work, exactly? If I'm reading it correctly, it would mean that fourth Attainments get more spell factors than second Attainments do. Is that intentional?<br /> <br /> Also, how compatible are Legacy Attainments with Arcana Attainments?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T11:32:21-07:00","id":889260,"title":"","content":"Okay, I understand what a Praxis <i>does</i> but I can't quite wrap my head around what a Praxis <i>is.</i> <br /> I get that they're supposed to be kinda proto-rotes but can I get an example or two aside from &quot;Pick a spell&quot;?<br /> Can they function like specialties or are they limited to specific spells that are created?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1838-danparadox","name":"danparadox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1838_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T14:19:09-07:00","id":889354,"title":"","content":"Fuego! from Harry Dresden (in)fame, would be a Praxis. It is a signature spell, one your mage uses time and time again and maybe is even known for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T16:34:17-07:00","id":889448,"title":"","content":"Does Mage Armor or more mundane armors protect against direct damage spells cast at Sensory range?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T17:19:55-07:00","id":889483,"title":"","content":"Ritual Casting and Teamwork Question:<br /> <br /> Do Sleepwalkers and Proximi participating in teamwork rituals all together count as one environmental Yantra (+1), p. 119, or does each individual participant count as separate environmental Yantra?<br /> <br /> For instance, if a mage is assisted by both a Sleepwalker and Proximi, would the spell have a +2 bonus and use up 2 Yantra slots, or would both people count as one Yantra for a +1 bonus?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T17:19:55-07:00","id":889484,"title":"","content":"(Reposting this from the ask-a-question thread - but if folks want to weigh in with unofficial answers over there go nuts, just don't want to clutter up the FAQ proper with chatter)<br /> <br /> How does Temporal Sympathy work?<br /> <br /> I assume that this line in the Attainment: &quot;<i>The spell is Withstood by the fragility of the temporal sympathy (p. 186) between the mage and her subject</i>&quot; is incorrect, as sympathy levels describe the similitude between the subject and its past self.<br /> <br /> 1.) What's the degree of connection between, say, a corpse and the moment it hit the ground? or a corpse and its own murder? Or a murder victim's corpse and an unrelated earlier event in the person's life? In the absence of a corpse can Postcognition target an empty crime scene or a memorial to the deceased?<br /> <br /> 2.) Can I apply it only to Time-related spells like Postcognition, or could I theoretically throw a Mind spell back in time so that someone that's bugging me right now decided to do something else earlier that day? Or a Death spell if I'm <i>really serious </i>about not wanting to be disturbed?<br /> <br /> 3.) The target of the spell is still the subject's present self, so I'm guessing that I can read where a car has been even if the past location isn't in the spell's range anymore, as long as the <i>present</i> car is in range?<br /> <br /> 4.) Likewise, they resist and/or Withstand with their present traits, unless their past had some sort of Time shielding up?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T23:09:20-07:00","id":889687,"title":"","content":"I agree with five eyes and would also like to knowhow u rule the spell Temporal Summoning page 190. It seems to imply that I can turn my enemies into babies wih no extra Whitstand or reach at all even against super naturals (we are discussing it on another topic). Also it does make no sense since there is the spell that does that with both Whitstand and a tons of extra reach to make it work ( rewrite history I think time 4). I think it might be an error for the errata thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T03:25:25-07:00","id":889773,"title":"","content":"Does the Potent Nimbus merit increase your effective Gnosis for determining the Nimbus Tilt beyond 10 or is it stuck at the 10 Gnosis limit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T05:22:16-07:00","id":889802,"title":"","content":"Hi guys<br /> <br /> I have a question about Withstanding, the book says &quot;Supernatural beings like mages, vampires, or demons do not add their Supernatural Tolerance trait to Withstand a spell&quot; and for spirits to use rank in most cases, but and for supernatural beings like Strix? they don't rave rank and their resistance trait can be really big.<br /> <br /> How will you handle with this kind of thing?<br /> <br /> Sorry for my bad english","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7761-glauber","name":"Glauber","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7761_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T09:04:35-07:00","id":889954,"title":"","content":"Mechanically, what does a brand new, freshly Awakened mage look like?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T09:51:22-07:00","id":889989,"title":"","content":"If a character with the Strained Condition suffers a Breaking Point but succeeds the roll and doesn't lose Integrity (so the Condition doesn't resolve), what happens? Does the Condition disappear without resolving? Does it remain but reset the penalty? Does it remain and retain the same penalty on their next Breaking Point roll?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T12:04:59-07:00","id":890063,"title":"","content":"So the term &quot;Rote Quality&quot; shows up a bunch in this book.<br /> <br /> The first instance is on page 92, where receives the text reads, &quot;the player the rote quality on the roll&quot; when discussing Clash of Wills and Scrutiny. There is no example to delineate what Rote Quality is or how it is determined. It appears later in the rules section under spells for adding Rote Quality rolls. In the Luck section, there is a rote that reads: The subject gains the rote quality on a number of mundane dice rolls equal to Potency. So here I'm thinking Rote Quality is a number. Later, in Time, it states that +1 Reach: For a point of Mana, Dodge actions taken while under this spell\u2019s effect have the rote quality. That reads like it isn't a number, but rather a condition? It isn't very clear.<br /> <br /> What is Rote quality, and where is it derived from?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11778-minightengale","name":"minightengale","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T13:26:28-07:00","id":890136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/880060-awakening-second-edition-faq-thread?p=889954#post889954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mechanically, what does a brand new, freshly Awakened mage look like?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dave mentioned it some time ago on 4chan. If I remember correctly, the stats are (in addition to standard mortal template and changes in it based on previous play before Awakening):<br /> <br /> One dot in one Ruling Arcanum, two dots in the other, one dot gained in a resistance attribute, Gnosis 1 and the relevant derivatives, Wisdom 7.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I intentionally didn't mention merits, because not only you should have at least 7 dots from before Awakening, which would mean you may get only three during Awakening, but you can also normally spend 5 dots to get 1 Gnosis, which should be only at one dot immediately after Awakening. This would imply that you had to earn those merit dots to get to at least 5 dots to be able to buy Gnosis with it and this implies training, not inherent ability gained during Awakening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5973,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","user":"Prometheus","date":". 05-13-2016, 04:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T13:34:59-07:00","id":890142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>minightengale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/880060-awakening-second-edition-faq-thread?p=890063#post890063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the term &quot;Rote Quality&quot; shows up a bunch in this book.<br /> <br /> The first instance is on page 92, where receives the text reads, &quot;the player the rote quality on the roll&quot; when discussing Clash of Wills and Scrutiny. There is no example to delineate what Rote Quality is or how it is determined. It appears later in the rules section under spells for adding Rote Quality rolls. In the Luck section, there is a rote that reads: The subject gains the rote quality on a number of mundane dice rolls equal to Potency. So here I'm thinking Rote Quality is a number. Later, in Time, it states that +1 Reach: For a point of Mana, Dodge actions taken while under this spell\u2019s effect have the rote quality. That reads like it isn't a number, but rather a condition? It isn't very clear.<br /> <br /> What is Rote quality, and where is it derived from?</div> </div> </div> </div>Like all other dice tricks, it's on page 214. It means &quot;reroll failed dice once.&quot;<br /> <br /> Rote quality actions have been in the Storytelling system since the first World of Darkness corebook, and they've been called that since then too. The idea was that mage's rotes would use them - but then, by the time Awakening 1e came out, they didn't (which was needlessly confusing). Some Fate spells in 1e granted the rote quality on dice rolls, Ochemata and other high-end Supernal beings had it on mundane tasks, that kind of thing.<br /> <br /> In 2e, if you're a master casting a rote you made yourself or a mage using a grimoire, rotes actually do now have the rote quality.<br /> <br /> <br /> So... It's a system term, that this is the 13th corebook to use, and is explained in the systems chapter.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T13:44:43-07:00","id":890149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/880060-awakening-second-edition-faq-thread?p=890142#post890142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like all other dice tricks, it's on page 214. It means &quot;reroll failed dice once.&quot;<br /> <br /> Rote quality actions have been in the Storytelling system since the first World of Darkness corebook, and they've been called that since then too. The idea was that mage's rotes would use them - but then, by the time Awakening 1e came out, they didn't (which was needlessly confusing). Some Fate spells in 1e granted the rote quality on dice rolls, Ochemata and other high-end Supernal beings had it on mundane tasks, that kind of thing.<br /> <br /> In 2e, if you're a master casting a rote you made yourself or a mage using a grimoire, rotes actually do now have the rote quality.<br /> <br /> <br /> So... It's a system term, that this is the 13th corebook to use, and is explained in the systems chapter.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Page 214 refers to &quot;Rote Actions,&quot; rather than &quot;Rote Quality,&quot; and that may account for some of the confusion by people unfamiliar with the mechanic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T21:29:41-07:00","id":890403,"title":"","content":"Do Dedicated tools and/or appropriate Artifacts qualify for the Path Tools &quot;trait&quot; of a mage's dream form, regardless of any other symbolic qualities? If so, are they duplicated in any mechanical sense besides reflexive access to the Yantra bonus?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T21:32:08-07:00","id":890404,"title":"","content":"Are spirits born of 'birth spirit' only around as long as the duration? The other creation spells list that their creation only lasts for the spells duration but birth spirit does not have that clause","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":