 clarification, when a spell relinquished with a willpower point falls apart over time, is it explicitly Paradox destroying the spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't seem to be explicitly spelled out as literally Paradox - if it was, there would probably be a line about how Guardians never, ever relinquish spells using a Willpower Point, since that's exactly the same as a Paradox when spellcasting except without any of the justifications for doing so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T14:50:28-07:00","id":890813,"title":"","content":"Any particular reason a 3 in each Ruling Arcana as a starting spread for Arcana isn't an option for a new character?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T20:55:54-07:00","id":890960,"title":"","content":"Is it intended that the penalty negation ability of Quantum Flux apply to spell casting rolls?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 201