onyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 05-15-2016, 03:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T14:05:05-07:00","id":891360,"title":"","content":"Can death 3 severe soul be used also against another supernatural being?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T23:10:44-07:00","id":891594,"title":"","content":"What incentive does a mage have to take Artifact over imbued item for something with more than 2 arcana? Artifacts seem to have lost their legendary status, mana regeneration, and enhanced durability they just seem to be more expensive imbued items<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10831-bauran","name":"Bauran","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10831_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T23:45:04-07:00","id":891599,"title":"","content":"I know this is a personal opinion, but I really didnt like the Egregore merit. <br /> <br /> I mean, isnt the real applicability of Egregore too restrictive? All other &quot;Order Special merits&quot; (Adamant Hand, Lex Magica, Masque and Techne) are not applicable only to one's order and offer benefits much more immediate or simply way better. <br /> <br /> Lets see the first level, Arche. It modifies the mage's contribution to teamwork spellcasting waiving the penalty for not having all arcana and providing a success if you do have all of them, but only if everyone is from The Mysterium (as Mysterium status is required, like other order merits). <br /> Comparing that to Techne, in which you can use a mundane focus as a tool AND, IF everyone is from Free Council, you get 8 again in teamwork spellcasting (for only one merit dot more), not only Egregore is weaker but really, really dificult to come into play. <br /> <br /> The other levels reflect the same experience as hardly ever coming into play. How many times did my mages go to another caucus or put to good use a deep connection to everyone on her order (while she already is in a sanctum anyway, so she already could affect them pretty well) without having to invest deeply in other merits such as status, contacts or mentor or a specific Space-based build? Seldom.<br /> <br /> How many times did I simply lose my magick tool in such desperation that would justify a 4 dot merit just to change it immediately? Never, and I wouldnt have this merit even if it happened often, for the -2 paradox and +1 yarna only. <br /> <br /> How many mage cabals with only Mysteriums I ever played? None. And when I play I am almost always the Mysteirum one, usually the only one. <br /> <br /> I get it Mysterium are more close-knitted than the other orders, but as a player I (and my RPG friends, from what I discussed with them) would never, ever use this merit, simply because it would almost never come into play and the benefits arent remotely good enough justify that, even in the rare cases that it would apply. And thats why I ask if it would be possible to change its applicability somehow, so that would be able to be applied in more stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11779-ungoliant","name":"Ungoliant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T00:01:53-07:00","id":891604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ungoliant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/880060-awakening-second-edition-faq-thread?p=891599#post891599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Comparing that to Techne, in which you can use a mundane focus as a tool AND, IF everyone is from Free Council, you get 8 again in teamwork spellcasting (for only one merit dot more), not only Egregore is weaker but really, really dificult to come into play.</div> </div> </div> </div>All mages must have Techne <i>with the same focus</i> to benefit from the 8-Again bonus. Simply being a member of the Free Council alone is insufficient.<br /> <br /> P. 104, &quot;If all mages casting a spell under the teamwork rules have this Merit representing the same focus, the leader\u2019s spellcasting roll gains 8-Again.&quot; <br /> <br /> I also don't know what you mean by &quot;for only one merit dot more.&quot; Techne is a two dot merit, must be purchased separated for each type of cultural practice, science or art form, and the merit is not included as part of Status (Free Council).<br /> <br /> The value of Egregore has been discussed extensively. If you wish to begin a new discussion now that the book has been released, a new and separate thread would be advisable. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T01:42:03-07:00","id":891621,"title":"","content":"<b>Advanced Scale Factor</b><br /> Most of the advanced scale factors start at a higher number than the Standard Factor, except Size. Why is this? Shouldn't it had been around 7 so that it can actually &quot;pay off&quot; to spend that Reach to increase advance the factor?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T02:09:51-07:00","id":891628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/880060-awakening-second-edition-faq-thread?p=891604#post891604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All mages must have Techne <i>with the same focus</i> to benefit from the 8-Again bonus. Simply being a member of the Free Council alone is insufficient.<br /> <br /> P. 104, &quot;If all mages casting a spell under the teamwork rules have this Merit representing the same focus, the leader\u2019s spellcasting roll gains 8-Again.&quot;<br /> <br /> I also don't know what you mean by &quot;for only one merit dot more.&quot; Techne is a two dot merit, must be purchased separated for each type of cultural practice, science or art form, and the merit is not included as part of Status (Free Council).<br /> <br /> The value of Egregore has been discussed extensively. If you wish to begin a new discussion now that the book has been released, a new and separate thread would be advisable.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am not talking only about merits cost here, but its usability in play.<br /> What I mean is that Techne (2 merit dots) has other uses even if not all participants are Free Councils, rewarding them randsomely with 8 again when they are (by &quot;being FC&quot; I mean &quot;being FC AND have this merit&quot;, as one could not have this merit and not be from FC, due to status requirement; it is not simply being FC) and have the same focus.<br /> Egregore Arche (1 merit dot) is only applicable when ALL participants are Mysterium (and have Egregore merit, so you cannot be from other order either).<br /> How often do we get a party with 3+ Mysterium without depending on other merits (like status,mentor, allies, etc) for this merit to be useful by itself?<br /> Similarly, I feel most other Egregore levels are Mysterium-driven and do not confer good ROI either.<br /> <br /> As I said, this is simply a personal opinion I would like to share. Others experiences might differ, of course, but I felt limited in what types of party composition this one would be useful, a limitation that does not exist in others order-special merits.<br /> I am not a developer and did not take part in previous discussions, but this is a FAQ thread, so as a customer I thought this would be an interesting place to understand the usability of this feature of the finished product.<br /> I might look into the previous discussions for this merit, sure, but as a principle I like to test and understand new products as they are before planning alternative rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11779,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11779-ungoliant","user":"Ungoliant","date":". 05-16-2016, 05:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11779-ungoliant","name":"Ungoliant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T03:41:09-07:00","id":891652,"title":"","content":"A Mage casts Exceptional Luck using Reach to get it as a Reflexive Action, and he wants to Combine it with another spell. Does it have to be a spell that also allows Reflexive casting somehow, or does the Exceptional Luck reach &quot;spread&quot; to combined spell as a whole?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T08:45:18-07:00","id":891764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bauran</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/880060-awakening-second-edition-faq-thread?p=891594#post891594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What incentive does a mage have to take Artifact over imbued item for something with more than 2 arcana? Artifacts seem to have lost their legendary status, mana regeneration, and enhanced durability they just seem to be more expensive imbued items</div> </div> </div> </div>Path tool bonus, no surcharge for Mana capacity, two-way Mana storage, higher inbuilt dicepool, safer Paradox handling, and the ability to have multiple effects go a long way.<br /> <br /> <br /> Is &quot;The Artifact has effective Arcana equal to the highest Arcanum used in its various effects&quot; meant as &quot;the Artifact has a uniform casting dicepool for all of its effects comprised of its Gnosis and a single uniform 'Arcanum' rating&quot; or &quot;each of an Artifact's effects has a dicepool comprised of its Gnosis and the highest Arcanum rating for that effect&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 05-16-2016, 11:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T10:08:44-07:00","id":891832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ungoliant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/880060-awakening-second-edition-faq-thread?p=891628#post891628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As I said, this is simply a personal opinion I would like to share. Others experiences might differ, of course, but I felt limited in what types of party composition this one would be useful, a limitation that does not exist in others order-special merits.<br /> I am not a developer and did not take part in previous discussions, but this is a FAQ thread, so as a customer I thought this would be an interesting place to understand the usability of this feature of the finished product.<br /> I might look into the previous discussions for this merit, sure, but as a principle I like to test and understand new products as they are before planning alternative rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>My previous comment wasn't meant to be dismissive of your opinions. <br /> <br /> However, a discussion about the comparative value of the Order merits is probably outside the more limited purview of this FAQ thread. I would encourage you to start a new thread on the topic. If the earlier debates about the Order merits from the 2e spoilers were indicative, it will be a very lively discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T10:48:21-07:00","id":891858,"title":"","content":"The Reach options on the Serendipity spell allow the Mage's player to substitute a dice pool that would help lead her towards a stated goal with another dice pool. Do these Reach options have no effect if the subject of the spell is someone other than the Mage?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T11:16:01-07:00","id":891873,"title":"","content":"If a mage casts a instant spell choosing High Speech as its only Yantra, does it take 2 turns or 1 turn to complete the cast?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11809-vilevader","name":"Vilevader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11809_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T14:02:57-07:00","id":891992,"title":"","content":"Upon joining a Legacy, characters will qualify for the first two Attainments. The first one is gained by joining the Legacy (and spending an Experience), which can then get a Praxis refund if you had that as a Praxis. I assume you then need to spend a second Experience on learning the second Attainment (meaning that even though Mages joining a Legacy qualify for the first two Attainments, they don't necessarily start with both Attainments unless they have extra Experience free at the time to spend on it)? Can you get the Praxis Arcane Beat refund if you have both of the Attainments as Praxes?<br /> <br /> Does the Optional Attainment accompanying each Attainment also need to be bought with Experience, and can you get a Praxis refund on those?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T16:01:49-07:00","id":892084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilevader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/880060-awakening-second-edition-faq-thread?p=891873#post891873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a mage casts a instant spell choosing High Speech as its only Yantra, does it take 2 turns or 1 turn to complete the cast?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 2. High Speech can't be reflexive. You just waste the other Yantra slot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts