rum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T23:58:50-07:00","id":893084,"title":"","content":"Hello, Spell under practice of Unveliling almost had a withstand trait, but knowing spell never. It is correct? I failed to grasp the reason around this <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T06:15:39-07:00","id":893235,"title":"","content":"How does someone end a tilt caused by an hex? If it is a supernatural being, can he heal an arm wreck or leg wreck tilt by simply spending mana or blood points ecc.. or does he suffer from the titl until the end of the hex? And what about a werewolf in gauru form? Will he automatically heal every tilt imposed on him ? (Since he regenerate all bashing and lethal each turn).<br /> By raw it seems as if regeneration and healing is useless against hexes and u suffer from them until the duration of the spell ends, since to heal from a tilt like arm wreck u have to heal the associated damage and then end the tilt/but the tilts caused by hexes are not related to any damage at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T17:29:16-07:00","id":893745,"title":"","content":"Piercing Earth (p.158) indicates that it's like Windstrike (p. 157) except that it effects the earth, rather than air or water; it does lethal/aggravted damage, which explains why it's Unraveling, and so 4 dots, but should using solid matter to attack be available with Windstrike (presumably with +1 Reach as per other similar spells)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4855-eggs-maledict","name":"Eggs Maledict","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T17:38:23-07:00","id":893750,"title":"","content":"Will we ever learn the fates of Phil, Cowl and Tallullah?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5958-logocentric","name":"Logocentric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T05:20:59-07:00","id":893954,"title":"","content":"How should Magic interact with Weapon Ratings? Should they be considered Equipment Bonus, or are they a different thing that needs different means to upgrade?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T07:07:15-07:00","id":893991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/880060-awakening-second-edition-faq-thread?p=893954#post893954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How should Magic interact with Weapon Ratings? Should they be considered Equipment Bonus, or are they a different thing that needs different means to upgrade?</div> </div> </div> </div>This. Still don't understand why matter on the spell list cannot improve weapons damage rating . Or how exactly monkey paw interacts with a gun or a knife ( equipment bonus on the attack roll?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T08:28:59-07:00","id":894036,"title":"","content":"If a Legacy does not (if they are allowed to) use a second arcanum from path to bolster their attainments, can the ruling arcanum of the legacy be used for this purpose? Does this, thematically, sound like using combined spells? Or are attainments still only one spell even with a secondary feature from another arcanum? Put another way, can the secondary arcanum of the legacy give effects radically different than the primary use of the attainment.<br /> Example--an attainment that dislodges sleeper souls AND causes bashing damage, but the legacy has no secondary arcanum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T08:31:30-07:00","id":894042,"title":"","content":"What exactly is a corpse for purposes of Death Magic? Is broken chair a Corpse of Chair? Can you ephemerally shape something into a corpse? For example, our Mage wants to create a zombie, so he goes into Twilight and Shapes some Ephemera into a Corpse, then targets it with Quicken Corpse, *then* pulls it out of Twilight. Is it a valid corpse for necromancing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T17:31:22-07:00","id":894459,"title":"","content":"Spell Stacking page 118<br /> &quot;Spell Stacking<br /> When multiple spells affect the same aspect of a character the<br /> effects of the spells do not stack, and instead the spell with the<br /> highest Potency takes effect. For example, a character benefitting<br /> from a spell that grants her +1 Strength casts a spell that grants<br /> her +3 Strength. The original spell with +1 Strength is suppressed<br /> for the Duration of the new spell. Both spell\u2019s Durations continue<br /> to lapse, though only the highest Potency spell is active.&quot;<br /> <br /> Due attainments count as spells for this rule?<br /> <br /> I mean like if you have one spell do one effect (defense) and the attainment provides another(armor) would that work. But what about Armor spell Armor attainment?<br /> <br /> Transient Stacking page 199<br /> &quot;Transient Stacking: Legacy Attainments may stack with spells,<br /> but only for a short time; doing so eradicates the spell, as the Attainment\u2019s<br /> intuitive, personal nature unravels the spell\u2019s Supernally<br /> charged Imago. Stacking a Legacy Attainment with a spell causes<br /> the spell\u2019s Duration to end, as if canceled, after one turn per dot<br /> the mage possesses in the spell\u2019s highest Arcanum or its usual<br /> Duration, whichever comes first.&quot;<br /> <br /> Does say you can stack it with spell effects, but Legacy attainments have a short grace period.<br /> <br /> The problem is why make the specification if attainments are already not apart of the spell stacking rule as written? Just asking for a little bit of clarifaction, as spell stacking says spells but attainments follow different rules<br /> <br /> page 192 first paragraph<br /> Attainments are magical effects, similar to spells but not subject<br /> to the same rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T23:10:56-07:00","id":894573,"title":"","content":"What happens if I fill a Gulmoth's corpus with letal damage? Does it get banished to the Abyss or just to the Shadow?<br /> <br /> What's the best combat use of Matter 3, Forces 2?<br /> <br /> What Arcana/Practice do I need to bring supernatural equipment (Artifacts, Fetishes, etc,) to the Astral?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T00:29:32-07:00","id":894596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/880060-awakening-second-edition-faq-thread?p=891832#post891832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My previous comment wasn't meant to be dismissive of your opinions.<br /> <br /> However, a discussion about the comparative value of the Order merits is probably outside the more limited purview of this FAQ thread. I would encourage you to start a new thread on the topic. If the earlier debates about the Order merits from the 2e spoilers were indicative, it will be a very lively discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As I said in my previous message, I am not talking about cost here, just citing it as a comparison tool. My point still is usability. <br /> And by all means if I ever start a discussion about alternative costs or rules for this merit this should not be here, but I am trying to understand the uability of this feature of the finished product as it is, in comparison to other order merits. <br /> <br /> I think first wI need to understand how this works and its usability, what was the developer team vision for its applicability and sich, before discussing it further in other threads.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11779-ungoliant","name":"Ungoliant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T09:21:00-07:00","id":894759,"title":"","content":"Charlequin once asked about Maskes inside Maskes, searching for a very cool concept; I was thinking about it and pondered about putting Shadow Name inside Masque-bestowed Merits. So, the question here would be:<br /> 1. Can you even do that?<br /> 2. If you do, is the protection bestowed by Shadow Name extended towards when Mage is not-in-the-Masque?<br /> Basically, Bob the Mage has a Persona of Alice the Shadowkiller. Bob has no Shadow Name merit, but Alice does; is Bob considered &quot;mundane persona&quot; for Alice's Shadow Name?<br /> 2a. As above, but: Bob the Mage has Shadow Name of Bob The Mage. Someone tries to check if Alice is Bob. Do their Shadow Names, well...stack for purposes of detection?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 05-20-2016, 12:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T11:25:25-07:00","id":894845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/880060-awakening-second-edition-faq-thread?p=894759#post894759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Charlequin once asked about Maskes inside Maskes, searching for a very cool concept; I was thinking about it and pondered about putting Shadow Name inside Masque-bestowed Merits. So, the question here would be:<br /> 1. Can you even do that?<br /> 2. If you do, is the protection bestowed by Shadow Name extended towards when Mage is not-in-the-Masque?<br /> Basically, Bob the Mage has a Persona of Alice the Shadowkiller. Bob has no Shadow Name merit, but Alice does; is Bob considered &quot;mundane persona&quot; for Alice's Shadow Name?<br /> 2a. As above, but: Bob the Mage has Shadow Name of Bob The Mage. Someone tries to check if Alice is Bob. Do their Shadow Names, well...stack for purposes of detection?</div> </div> </div> </div>Bob=&gt;Alice=&gt;The ShadowKiller<br /> No Alice is the Mundane id of ShadowKiller. Apply the benefit of ShadowName to Alice.<br /> <br /> Bob=&gt;BobTheMage<br /> Bob=&gt;Alice=&gt;TheShadowKiller<br /> No the protections can't stack because they're on different branches. The only protection is the protection provided by the Masque merit.<br /> <br /> NOW if you wanted to figure out IF BoTheMage is Alice Then we have something<br /> <br /> BobTheMage&lt;=Bob=&gt;Alice<br /> Then they might. and actually I'd say, the protection of masque and the shadow name apply.<br /> <br /> Likewise trying to figure out is BobTheMage is TheShadowKiller<br /> BobTheMage&lt;=Bob=&gt;Alice=&gt;TheShadowKiller<br /> You would be breaking through the shadowname, the masque, and the second shadowname","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":11731,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","user":"MercSet","date":".  One more explaination branch 05-20-2016, 02:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T17:40:34-07:00","id":895175,"title":"","content":"Couple of Space questions:<br /> <br /> Which Connection is used is for Withstanding Borrow Threads, the link that the Mage is trying to transfer?<br /> <br /> Does a picture of something have an inherent sympathetic connection to it -besides- being useful for a sympathetic yantra?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T17:50:04-07:00","id":895180,"title":"","content":"Shouldn't Time 3 Temporal Summoning have a Withstand rating besides temporal sympathy, just like Time 4 Rewrite History? Also, is Temporal Summoning also a Patterning Practice, not Weaving?<br /> <br /> Without spending any of the listed discretionary Reach, does Rewrite History only change narrative aspects of a character or subject?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T18:43:13-07:00","id":895201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MercSet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/880060-awakening-second-edition-faq-thread?p=894845#post894845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Bob=&gt;Alice=&gt;The ShadowKiller<br /> No Alice is the Mundane id of ShadowKiller. Apply the benefit of ShadowName to Alice.<br /> <br /> Bob=&gt;BobTheMage<br /> Bob=&gt;Alice=&gt;TheShadowKiller<br /> No the protections can't stack because they're on different branches. The only protection is the protection provided by the Masque merit.<br /> <br /> NOW if you wanted to figure out IF BoTheMage is Alice Then we have something<br /> <br /> BobTheMage&lt;=Bob=&gt;Alice<br /> Then they might. and actually I'd say, the protection of masque and the shadow name apply.<br /> <br /> Likewise trying to figure out is BobTheMage is TheShadowKiller<br /> BobTheMage&lt;=Bob=&gt;Alice=&gt;TheShadowKiller<br /> You would be breaking through the shadowname, the masque, and the second shadowname</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like this explanation a lot.Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T16:11:21-07:00","id":895729,"title":"","content":"So scribe grimoire can't benifit from scale factor (multiple targets), has no notable use of potency and with a reach is lasting. My question is doesnt scribe grimoire seem more like an attainment than a spell since it does not benifit from spell factors including the free ones if you use the reach option?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T09:14:44-07:00","id":896109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/880060-awakening-second-edition-faq-thread?p=894759#post894759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Charlequin once asked about Maskes inside Maskes, searching for a very cool concept; I was thinking about it and pondered about putting Shadow Name inside Masque-bestowed Merits. So, the question here would be:<br /> 1. Can you even do that?<br /> 2. If you do, is the protection bestowed by Shadow Name extended towards when Mage is not-in-the-Masque?<br /> Basically, Bob the Mage has a Persona of Alice the Shadowkiller. Bob has no Shadow Name merit, but Alice does; is Bob considered &amp;quot;mundane persona&amp;quot; for Alice's Shadow Name?<br /> 2a. As above, but: Bob the Mage has Shadow Name of Bob The Mage. Someone tries to check if Alice is Bob. Do their Shadow Names, well...stack for purposes of detection?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's funny, this is exactly how I adjusted the character once it was pointed out to me that the text specifically forbids taking additional Masques with the free dots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T10:01:09-07:00","id":896126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/880060-awakening-second-edition-faq-thread?p=895729#post895729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So scribe grimoire can't benifit from scale factor (multiple targets), has no notable use of potency and with a reach is lasting. My question is doesnt scribe grimoire seem more like an attainment than a spell since it does not benifit from spell factors including the free ones if you use the reach option?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can only scribe one spell, but there's nothing stopping you from scribing it multiple times into multiple grimoires, that's what I would use Scale for. I'd allow a Reach cost that scribes it into multiple forms of media.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T11:56:31-07:00","id":896203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/880060-awakening-second-edition-faq-thread?p=896126#post896126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can only scribe one spell, but there's nothing stopping you from scribing it multiple times into multiple grimoires, that's what I would use Scale for. I'd allow a Reach cost that scribes it into multiple forms of media.</div> </div> </div> </div>D'oh I read that as you can only scribe one spell into a grimoire in one instance. Of course if you were to do more than one instance it'd have to be writing the same spell. That makes sense for it to have meant that, thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T13:21:59-07:00","id":896257,"title":"","content":"Hey guys, so question? You shadow names are like taking on an identity right. so if you take the ID of a tragic hero(Hamlet comes to mind) Can and if so at what level; Can Fate Arcane nudge the fate of the ShadowName to befall the character?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T13:36:04-07:00","id":896270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MercSet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/880060-awakening-second-edition-faq-thread?p=896257#post896257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey guys, so question? You shadow names are like taking on an identity right. so if you take the ID of a tragic hero(Hamlet comes to mind) Can and if so at what level; Can Fate Arcane nudge the fate of the ShadowName to befall the character?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I guess it would be a normal Fate spell, but I would let you use their Shadow Name as a Yantra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T17:04:21-07:00","id":896397,"title":"","content":"Can the Prime 2 spell &quot;Invisible Runes&quot; be used to create a valid Yantra for runic casting?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T19:24:49-07:00","id":896462,"title":"","content":"We're already having minor disagreements about this point, and I think it's pretty important for actual play, so:<br /> <br /> The Clash of Wills section says that Mages are always aware when their spells clash, but -how- aware they are has come up at our table because of Veiling magic. The best example I can use is Cloak Nimbus vs Supernal Vision - the first is explicitly there to protect against the second, but because of the Clash rules, isn't the person who casted Supernal Vision consciously aware that their magic ran afoul of -something- and has a clue that even if the spell reported back that nothing was wrong, there -has- to be something there? Otherwise, Supernal Vision wouldn't have clashed against anything!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":451,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","user":"Kirby Jerusalem","date":". 05-22-2016, 10:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T06:12:50-07:00","id":896732,"title":"","content":"Quantum Flux the first level Fate spell. It can negate penalties on actions. What stops it from negating spell casting penalties? From a players point it is good. I see nothing wrong with it though I am told it is too powerful for level one. I do like it though. From a Storytellers viewpoint, I also see nothing wrong with it,but I am new to storytelling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T09:35:39-07:00","id":896874,"title":"","content":"Do penalties to Medicine rolls from Dark Eras apply to rotes using Medicine?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T11:02:26-07:00","id":896966,"title":"","content":"I can't find it, I don't <i>think</i> this has been asked yet, but how does Advanced Potency and regular Potency interact with Dispel Magic from Prime 1 and Supernal Dispellation from Prime 4?<br /> <br /> The way it is written, Dispel is Withstood by the arcana rating of the caster when they cast the spell, and the Potency of the Dispellation spells are the primary spellfactor. This <i>implies</i> I think, that the potency of the victim's spell has nothing to do with the Withstand or how powerful the Dispel has to be. But, Advanced Potency is listed under Potency and adds +2 to the Withstand of spells trying to resist being dispelled.<br /> <br /> So that implies that a spell with potency 1 or potency 20 from a Master are both likely to be Dispelled by anyone with Prime 1 and the other arcana dots needed, provided they can foot a potency 6 Dispellation and enough reach to pull this off as Lasting. But, with the Advanced Potency reach, the Withstand is like, what, 7 now? And then the opposing Mage needs a Dispel with 8 potency.<br /> <br /> If I understood all this correctly, this means that a Supernal Dispellation with Potency 8 will kill any pre-archmaster spell they come across, without fail. Have I understood this correctly?<br /> <br /> (reference pages: 113, 170.)<br /> <br /> Edit: I guess I also need to know how Dispel and advanced potency interact with Wards and Signs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","user":"Scarlet Witch","date":". 05-23-2016, 02:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T11:22:11-07:00","id":896993,"title":"","content":"Say, I have Life 2+, Fate 2+ and a Familiar Claiming a body. I tatoo runes of Body Control on the body; can Body Control have a Conditional Duration of &quot;while the runes are whole&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T11:26:00-07:00","id":896998,"title":"","content":"Does a Familiar that has become a Claimed even remain a familiar without some special additional magic? It's no longer a spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avata